window.SOURATE_DATA = {"numSourate":23,"nomSourate":"Al-Mu'minun","nomFr":"Les croyants","nomEn":"The Believers","nomArabe":"المؤمنون","lieu":"La Mecque","lieuEn":"Makkah","typeSourateLabel":"Sourate Mecquoise","typeSourateLabelEn":"Meccan Surah","typeSourateClasse":"mecquoise","ordreRev":74,"nbVersets":118,"versets":[{"numVerset":1,"texteArabe":"بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيمِ قَدْ أَفْلَحَ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ","tradPropre":"Bienheureux sont certes les croyants,","tradEn":"Certainly will the believers have succeeded:","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ceux qui croient en Allah et qui mettent Ses lois en pratique connaîtront le succès: ils obtiendront ce qu’ils recherchent et échapperont à ce qu’ils redoutent.","explicationEn":"1. Those who believed in Allah and acted according to His laws have indeed succeeded by achieving whatever they sought, and gaining salvation from whatever they feared.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023001","lienPrecedent":"sourate-22-verset-78.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-2.html"},{"numVerset":2,"texteArabe":"الَّذِينَ هُمْ فِي صَلَاتِهِمْ خَاشِعُونَ","tradPropre":"ceux qui sont humbles dans leur Salât,","tradEn":"They who are during their prayer humbly intent","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ceux-ci sont pleins d’humilité durant leur prière: leur corps est apaisé et immobile, leur cœur est serein et vide de toute autre préoccupation.","explicationEn":"2. Those who were humble in their prayer: their limbs remained calm during it and their hearts were free of distractions.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023002","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-1.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-3.html"},{"numVerset":3,"texteArabe":"وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ عَنِ اللَّغْوِ مُعْرِضُونَ","tradPropre":"qui se détournent des futilités,","tradEn":"And they who turn away from ill speech","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils refusent, par les paroles ou les actes, tout ce qui a trait au faux, aux futilités et à la désobéissance.","explicationEn":"3. Those who turned away from falsehood and futility, especially those futile actions and speech which was sinful.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023003","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-2.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-4.html"},{"numVerset":4,"texteArabe":"وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ لِلزَّكَاةِ فَاعِلُونَ","tradPropre":"qui s'acquittent de la Zakât,","tradEn":"And they who are observant of zakāh","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Afin de se purifier des péchés et de purifier leurs richesses, ils en prélèvent l’aumône légale.","explicationEn":"4. Those who purified themselves of evil characteristics, and their wealth by taking out Zakat from it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023004","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-3.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-5.html"},{"numVerset":5,"texteArabe":"وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ لِفُرُوجِهِمْ حَافِظُونَ","tradPropre":"et qui préservent leurs sexes [de tout rapport],","tradEn":"And they who guard their private parts","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils sont chastes et purs, puisqu’ils refusent d’avoir des rapports charnels illicites comme la fornication, la sodomie et les autres turpitudes.","explicationEn":"5. Those who safeguarded their private parts by keeping them far from fornication, homosexuality and shameful actions; so they remained pure and chaste.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023005","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-4.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-6.html"},{"numVerset":6,"texteArabe":"إِلَّا عَلَىٰ أَزْوَاجِهِمْ أَوْ مَا مَلَكَتْ أَيْمَانُهُمْ فَإِنَّهُمْ غَيْرُ مَلُومِينَ","tradPropre":"si ce n'est qu'avec leurs épouses ou les esclaves qu'ils possèdent, car là vraiment, on ne peut les blâmer;","tradEn":"Except from their wives or those their right hands possess, for indeed, they will not be blamed -","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils n’ont de rapports charnels qu’avec leurs épouses ou les esclaves qu’ils possèdent et ces rapports ne sont pas répréhensibles.","explicationEn":"6. Except using them with their wives or the female servants they possessed, for they are blameless in taking pleasure from them through sexual intercourse and the like.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023006","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-5.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-7.html"},{"numVerset":7,"texteArabe":"فَمَنِ ابْتَغَىٰ وَرَاءَ ذَالِكَ فَأُولَائِكَ هُمُ الْعَادُونَ","tradPropre":"alors que ceux qui cherchent au-delà de ces limites sont des transgresseurs;","tradEn":"But whoever seeks beyond that, then those are the transgressors -","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Quiconque cherche à avoir des rapports charnels avec des femmes autres que ses épouses ou les esclaves qu’il possède, outrepasse les limites d’Allah et va au-delà de ce qu’Il lui permet.","explicationEn":"7. So whosoever seeks pleasure from other than his wives and female servants that he possesses, he is transgressing the limits of Allah by delving into that which Allah has forbidden, without keeping to that which He has kept lawful.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023007","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-6.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-8.html"},{"numVerset":8,"texteArabe":"وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ لِأَمَانَاتِهِمْ وَعَهْدِهِمْ رَاعُونَ","tradPropre":"et qui veillent à la sauvegarde des dépôts confiés à eux et honorent leurs engagements,","tradEn":"And they who are to their trusts and their promises attentive","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les croyants sauvegardent également les dépôts que leur confie Allah et ceux que leur confient les gens. Ils tiennent leurs engagements et ne les trahissent pas.","explicationEn":"8. Those who fulfil and do not neglect or usurp the trusts Allah has entrusted them with, or any of His servants have entrusted them with. Rather, they keep to their pacts.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023008","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-7.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-9.html"},{"numVerset":9,"texteArabe":"وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ عَلَىٰ صَلَوَاتِهِمْ يُحَافِظُونَ","tradPropre":"et qui observent strictement leur Salât.","tradEn":"And they who carefully maintain their prayers -","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils sont assidus dans leurs prières qu’ils accomplissent dans les intervalles de temps qui leur sont imparties et en en respectant strictement les piliers, les obligations et les rites recommandés.","explicationEn":"9. Those who observe their prayers by being punctual in them, by performing them at their correct times together, obligations and preferred actions.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023009","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-8.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-10.html"},{"numVerset":10,"texteArabe":"أُولَائِكَ هُمُ الْوَارِثُونَ","tradPropre":"Ce sont eux les héritiers,","tradEn":"Those are the inheritors","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ceux qui détiennent ces caractéristiques seront les héritiers.","explicationEn":"10. Those possessing these characteristics are the true inheritors.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023010","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-9.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-11.html"},{"numVerset":11,"texteArabe":"الَّذِينَ يَرِثُونَ الْفِرْدَوْسَ هُمْ فِيهَا خَالِدُونَ","tradPropre":"qui hériteront le Paradis pour y demeurer éternellement.","tradEn":"Who will inherit al-Firdaus. They will abide therein eternally.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils hériteront du Paradis où ils séjourneront éternellement et où les délices ne s’interrompent jamais.","explicationEn":"11. They will inherit the loftiest level of paradise wherein they will live forever. Their bounties will not finish in it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023011","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-10.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-12.html"},{"numVerset":12,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا الْإِنْسَانَ مِنْ سُلَالَةٍ مِنْ طِينٍ","tradPropre":"Nous avons certes créé l'homme d'un extrait d'argile.","tradEn":"And certainly did We create man from an extract of clay.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons créé Adam, le père des humains, d’une argile prélevée d’un mélange d’eau et de terre.","explicationEn":"12. Verily, I created the father of mankind, Adam, from clay. I took the soil he was created from, from a mixture of water and the soil of the earth.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023012","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-11.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-13.html"},{"numVerset":13,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ جَعَلْنَاهُ نُطْفَةً فِي قَرَارٍ مَكِينٍ","tradPropre":"puis Nous en fîmes une goutte de sperme dans un reposoir solide.","tradEn":"Then We placed him as a sperm-drop in a firm lodging [i.e., the womb].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Puis Nous avons créé sa descendance d’une goutte de sperme qui se maintient dans l’utérus jusqu’à l’accouchement.","explicationEn":"13. Then I created his progeny who procreate, by way of a drop of sperm that lodges in the womb until birth.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023013","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-12.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-14.html"},{"numVerset":14,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ خَلَقْنَا النُّطْفَةَ عَلَقَةً فَخَلَقْنَا الْعَلَقَةَ مُضْغَةً فَخَلَقْنَا الْمُضْغَةَ عِظَامًا فَكَسَوْنَا الْعِظَامَ لَحْمًا ثُمَّ أَنْشَأْنَاهُ خَلْقًا آخَرَ  فَتَبَارَكَ اللَّهُ أَحْسَنُ الْخَالِقِينَ","tradPropre":"Ensuite, Nous avons fait du sperme une adhérence; et de l'adhérence Nous avons créé un embryon; puis, de cet embryon Nous avons créé des os et Nous avons revêtu les os de chair. Ensuite, Nous l'avons transformé en une tout autre création. Gloire à Allah le Meilleur des créateurs!","tradEn":"Then We made the sperm-drop into a clinging clot, and We made the clot into a lump [of flesh], and We made [from] the lump, bones, and We covered the bones with flesh; then We developed him into another creation. So blessed is Allāh, the best of creators.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> En y insufflant la vie, expliquent nombre d’exégètes.","explicationUnanime":"De cette goutte de sperme, Nous faisons une adhérence rouge que Nous transformons en un bout de chair mâchée qui devient un amas d’os durs. Nous enveloppons ensuite ces derniers de chair puis Nous en faisons une créature indépendante après y avoir insufflé l’esprit et lui avoir donné vie. Gloire à Allah donc, le Meilleur des créateurs.","explicationEn":"14. I then created the lodged drop of sperm into a red clot of blood, which I then created into a piece of flesh, which I then created into hard bones. I then covered those bones with flesh and then developed it into a completely different creation, by blowing a soul into it and bringing it out into life. Praised is Allah, the best of creators!","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":{"titre":"Signe Embryologique — Les étapes successives de la formation du fœtus","titreEn":"Embryological Sign — The Successive Stages of Fetal Development","resume":"Description chronologique des stades : goutte (Nutfah), adhérence ('Alaqah), morceau de chair mâchée (Mudghah), ossature ('Idhām) puis enveloppement par la chair (Lahm).","resumeEn":"Chronological description of the stages: drop (Nutfah), clinging substance ('Alaqah), chewed-like lump (Mudghah), bones ('Idhām), then clothing the bones with flesh (Lahm).","developpement":"\n      <p><strong>L'ordre exact des stades embryonnaires :</strong> Ce verset détaille avec une terminologie précise la transformation graduelle dans l'utérus : de la goutte (<em>Nutfah</em>) à l'adhérence (<em>'Alaqah</em>) qui s'implante dans la paroi utérine, puis à la <em>Mudghah</em> (substance ayant l'aspect d'une chair mâchée portant l'empreinte des dents, semblable aux somites de l'embryon), suivie de la formation du squelette cartilagineux puis de son habillage par les muscles.</p>\n    ","developpementEn":"\n      <p><strong>Exact Sequence of Embryonic Stages:</strong> This verse details the gradual transformation in the womb: from the drop (<em>Nutfah</em>) to the clinging stage (<em>'Alaqah</em>), then the <em>Mudghah</em> (resembling chewed flesh with tooth-like somite impressions), followed by the skeletal framework and its enveloping with muscles.</p>\n    "},"codeAudio":"023014","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-13.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-15.html"},{"numVerset":15,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ إِنَّكُمْ بَعْدَ ذَالِكَ لَمَيِّتُونَ","tradPropre":"Et puis, après cela vous mourrez.","tradEn":"Then indeed, after that you are to die.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô gens, après être passés par toutes ces étapes et que vos durées de vie s’écoulent, vous mourrez.","explicationEn":"15. O people! After having passed through all these phases, you shall die when your lives expire.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023015","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-14.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-16.html"},{"numVerset":16,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ إِنَّكُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ تُبْعَثُونَ","tradPropre":"Et puis au Jour de la Résurrection vous serez ressuscités.","tradEn":"Then indeed you, on the Day of Resurrection, will be resurrected.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Puis après votre mort, vous serez ressuscités de vos tombes le Jour de la Résurrection afin de rendre des comptes pour les œuvres que vous avez accomplies dans le bas monde.","explicationEn":"16. Then, after your death, you shall be resurrected from your graves on the Day of Judgment so that you may be held to account for whatever deeds you sent forth.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023016","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-15.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-17.html"},{"numVerset":17,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا فَوْقَكُمْ سَبْعَ طَرَائِقَ وَمَا كُنَّا عَنِ الْخَلْقِ غَافِلِينَ","tradPropre":"Nous avons créé, au-dessus de vous, sept cieux. Et Nous ne sommes pas inattentifs à la création.","tradEn":"And We have created above you seven layered heavens, and never have We been of [Our] creation unaware.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô gens, Nous avons créé au-dessus de vous sept cieux successifs. Nous ne sommes pas inattentifs à ce que Nous créons ni ne l’oublions.","explicationEn":"17. O people! Verily, I created seven heavens over you, one above the other. I am never neglectful of My creation, nor am I One to forget it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023017","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-16.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-18.html"},{"numVerset":18,"texteArabe":"وَأَنْزَلْنَا مِنَ السَّمَاءِ مَاءً بِقَدَرٍ فَأَسْكَنَّاهُ فِي الْأَرْضِ  وَإِنَّا عَلَىٰ ذَهَابٍ بِهِ لَقَادِرُونَ","tradPropre":"Et Nous avons fait descendre l'eau du ciel avec mesure. Puis Nous l'avons maintenue dans la terre, cependant que Nous sommes bien Capable de la faire disparaître.","tradEn":"And We have sent down rain from the sky in a measured amount and settled it in the earth. And indeed, We are Able to take it away.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous faisons descendre du Ciel l’eau de la pluie en des quantités répondant à la nécessité: ni trop, pour qu’elle ne soit pas préjudiciable, ni trop peu, pour qu’elle réponde aux besoins. Nous faisons en sorte que cette eau reste dans la terre afin que les gens et les animaux s’en servent à leur profit, sachant que Nous sommes capables de la faire disparaître et vous ne pourriez plus alors en faire usage.","explicationEn":"18. I sent down rain from the heavens according to the need toward it; not in excessive amounts that cause ruin, nor too little that is insufficient. I allow it to settle on earth so that the people and animals can take benefit from it. Otherwise, I am capable of causing it to wash away, in which case they would not be able to benefit from it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023018","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-17.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-19.html"},{"numVerset":19,"texteArabe":"فَأَنْشَأْنَا لَكُمْ بِهِ جَنَّاتٍ مِنْ نَخِيلٍ وَأَعْنَابٍ لَكُمْ فِيهَا فَوَاكِهُ كَثِيرَةٌ وَمِنْهَا تَأْكُلُونَ","tradPropre":"Avec elle, Nous avons produit pour vous des jardins de palmiers et de vignes, dans lesquels vous avez des fruits abondants et desquels vous mangez,","tradEn":"And We brought forth for you thereby gardens of palm trees and grapevines in which for you are abundant fruits and from which you eat.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"A partir de cette eau, Nous avons produit pour vous des jardins plantés de palmiers et de vignes qui vous donnent des fruits divers aux formes et aux couleurs variées, comme les figues, les grenades et les pommes. Et c’est de ces fruits que vous vous nourrissez.","explicationEn":"19. Through that water I then created gardens for you, the like of palms and grapevines. You have fruits of varying colours and appearance that grow within them, like figs, pomegranates and apples, of which you eat.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023019","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-18.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-20.html"},{"numVerset":20,"texteArabe":"وَشَجَرَةً تَخْرُجُ مِنْ طُورِ سَيْنَاءَ تَنْبُتُ بِالدُّهْنِ وَصِبْغٍ لِلْآكِلِينَ","tradPropre":"ainsi qu'un arbre (l'olivier) qui pousse au Mont Sinaî, en produisant l'huile servant à oindre et où les mangeurs trempent leur pain.","tradEn":"And [We brought forth] a tree issuing from Mount Sinai which produces oil and food [i.e., olives] for those who eat.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Ou : né sur le mont Sinaï. Il s’agit de l’olivier.","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons aussi produit pour vous à partir de cette eau des oliviers qui poussent dans le Mont Sinaï et dont les fruits donnent une huile servant d'onction pour le corps ou de nourriture lorsqu’on y trempe son pain.","explicationEn":"20. Through that water, I also created the olive tree for you, the origins of which come from the land of Mount Sinai. From its fruits, the oil is extracted which you use and consume.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023020","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-19.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-21.html"},{"numVerset":21,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّ لَكُمْ فِي الْأَنْعَامِ لَعِبْرَةً  نُسْقِيكُمْ مِمَّا فِي بُطُونِهَا وَلَكُمْ فِيهَا مَنَافِعُ كَثِيرَةٌ وَمِنْهَا تَأْكُلُونَ","tradPropre":"Vous avez certes dans les bestiaux, un sujet de méditation. Nous vous donnons à boire de ce qu'ils ont dans le ventre, et vous y trouvez également maintes utilités; et vous vous en nourrissez.","tradEn":"And indeed, for you in livestock is a lesson. We give you drink from that which is in their bellies, and for you in them are numerous benefits, and from them you eat.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô gens, vous trouvez assurément dans les bestiaux (camelins, bovins, ovins et caprins) des signes qui vous donnent une idée du pouvoir d’Allah et de la sollicitude dont Il vous entoure. En effet, Nous vous abreuvons du lait pur et comestible que contient le ventre de ces bêtes et vous tirez profit de ces dernières de différentes manières. Ainsi, elles vous servent de montures, vous produisent de la laine et des poils et de plus, vous vous nourrissez de leur viande.","explicationEn":"21. O people! Indeed, you have a lesson to take from grazing livestock (camels, cows and sheep), in that you can draw conclusions from them in the power of Allah and His kindness to you. He quenches your thirst with pure, tasty milk from the bellies of these animals. You can also derive other benefits from them, like conveyance, wool, fur, bristles, together with being able to consume their meat.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023021","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-20.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-22.html"},{"numVerset":22,"texteArabe":"وَعَلَيْهَا وَعَلَى الْفُلْكِ تُحْمَلُونَ","tradPropre":"Sur eux ainsi que sur des vaisseaux vous êtes transportés.","tradEn":"And upon them and on ships you are carried.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Sur la terre ferme, ce sont les dromadaires qui vous servent de vaisseaux et sur mer, ce sont les bateaux.","explicationEn":"22. You are carried on the camels on land and on the ships at sea.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023022","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-21.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-23.html"},{"numVerset":23,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ أَرْسَلْنَا نُوحًا إِلَىٰ قَوْمِهِ فَقَالَ يَا قَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِنْ إِلَاهٍ غَيْرُهُ  أَفَلَا تَتَّقُونَ","tradPropre":"Nous envoyâmes Noé vers son peuple. Il dit: «O mon peuple, adorez Allah. Vous n'avez pas d'autre divinité en dehors de Lui. Ne [Le] craignez-vous pas?»","tradEn":"And We had certainly sent Noah to his people, and he said, \"O my people, worship Allāh; you have no deity other than Him; then will you not fear Him?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons envoyé Noé à son peuple afin de les appeler à adorer Allah. Il leur dit: Ô mon peuple, adorez Allah Seul car vous n’avez d’autre dieu méritant d’être adoré que Lui. Ne le craindrez-vous donc pas en vous conformant à Ses commandements et en renonçant à ce qu’Il vous a défendu?","explicationEn":"23. Indeed, I sent Noah (peace be upon him) to his people to call them towards Allah, so he said to them, “O my people! Worship Allah only; you do not have any true deity except Him, may He be glorified. Will you not be mindful of Allah by fulfilling His commands and refraining from His prohibitions?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023023","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-22.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-24.html"},{"numVerset":24,"texteArabe":"فَقَالَ الْمَلَأُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا مِنْ قَوْمِهِ مَا هَاذَا إِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِثْلُكُمْ يُرِيدُ أَنْ يَتَفَضَّلَ عَلَيْكُمْ وَلَوْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ لَأَنْزَلَ مَلَائِكَةً مَا سَمِعْنَا بِهَاذَا فِي آبَائِنَا الْأَوَّلِينَ","tradPropre":"Alors les notables de son peuple qui avaient mécru dirent: «Celui-ci n'est qu'un être humain comme vous voulant se distinguer à votre détriment. Si Allah avait voulu, ce sont des Anges qu'Il aurait fait descendre. Jamais nous n'avons entendu cela chez nos ancêtres les plus reculés.","tradEn":"But the eminent among those who disbelieved from his people said, \"This is not but a man like yourselves who wishes to take precedence over you; and if Allāh had willed [to send a messenger], He would have sent down angels. We have not heard of this among our forefathers.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Qu’un homme ait été envoyé comme Messager ou que seul Allah doive être adoré.","explicationUnanime":"Les nobles et les chefs mécréants de son peuple dirent à leurs subordonnés et aux gens ordinaires: Celui qui prétend être un messager n’est qu’un être humain comme vous, et son but est de devenir votre chef. Si Allah voulait nous envoyer un messager, Il nous aurait envoyé un ange et non un humain. Jamais nous n’avons entendu ce qu’il prétend chez nos aïeux les plus anciens.","explicationEn":"24. So the noblemen and leaders from his people who disbelieved in Allah said to their followers and the masses, “This man that claims to be a messenger is only a human like yourselves; he only desires leadership and rule over you. If Allah wished to send a messenger to you He would have done so by sending one from the angels, not from the humans. We have not heard anything like what he is claiming from our predecessors!”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023024","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-23.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-25.html"},{"numVerset":25,"texteArabe":"إِنْ هُوَ إِلَّا رَجُلٌ بِهِ جِنَّةٌ فَتَرَبَّصُوا بِهِ حَتَّىٰ حِينٍ","tradPropre":"Ce n'est en vérité qu'un homme atteint de folie, observez-le donc durant quelque temps.","tradEn":"He is not but a man possessed with madness, so wait concerning him for a time.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Noé n’est qu’un aliéné qui n’est pas conscient de ce qu’il dit. Observez ses faits et gestes afin que cette vérité apparaisse aux gens.","explicationEn":"25. He is only a man who is mad. He does not understand what he himself is saying. Wait and see when soon his true reality becomes apparent to the people.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023025","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-24.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-26.html"},{"numVerset":26,"texteArabe":"قَالَ رَبِّ انْصُرْنِي بِمَا كَذَّبُونِ","tradPropre":"Il dit: «Seigneur! Apporte-moi secours parce qu'ils me traitent de menteur».","tradEn":"[Noah] said, \"My Lord, support me because they have denied me.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Noé dit: Ô mon Seigneur, secours-moi contre eux et venge-moi d’eux pour m’avoir démenti.","explicationEn":"26. Noah (peace be upon him) said, “O my Lord! Help me against them and pay them back for their rejection and defiance!”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023026","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-25.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-27.html"},{"numVerset":27,"texteArabe":"فَأَوْحَيْنَا إِلَيْهِ أَنِ اصْنَعِ الْفُلْكَ بِأَعْيُنِنَا وَوَحْيِنَا فَإِذَا جَاءَ أَمْرُنَا وَفَارَ التَّنُّورُ  فَاسْلُكْ فِيهَا مِنْ كُلٍّ زَوْجَيْنِ اثْنَيْنِ وَأَهْلَكَ إِلَّا مَنْ سَبَقَ عَلَيْهِ الْقَوْلُ مِنْهُمْ  وَلَا تُخَاطِبْنِي فِي الَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا  إِنَّهُمْ مُغْرَقُونَ","tradPropre":"Nous lui révélâmes: «Construis l'arche sous Nos yeux et selon Notre révélation. Et quand Notre commandement viendra et que le four bouillonnera, achemine là-dedans un couple de chaque espèce, ainsi que ta famille, sauf ceux d'entre eux contre qui la parole a déjà été prononcée; et ne t'adresse pas à Moi au sujet des injustes, car ils seront fatalement noyés.","tradEn":"So We inspired to him, \"Construct the ship under Our observation and Our inspiration, and when Our command comes and the oven overflows, put into it [i.e., the ship] from each [creature] two mates and your family, except him for whom the decree [of destruction] has proceeded. And do not address Me concerning those who have wronged; indeed, they are to be drowned.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> La femme de Noé et l’un de ses fils, selon certains commentateurs.","explicationUnanime":"Nous lui avons alors révélé de construire le bateau sous Notre observation et conformément à ce que Nous lui avons enseigné puis lorsque sera émis Notre ordre de les anéantir et que l’eau bouillonnera dans le four, fais alors entrer dans ce bateau un couple de chaque espèce vivante afin qu’aucune de ces espèces ne disparaisse et fais également entrer ta famille sauf ceux que Nous avons condamné à l’anéantissement à l’image de ton épouse et de ton fils. Ne plaide pas en faveur de ceux qui en mécroyant se sont rendus injustes car ils seront irrémédiablement noyés dans le Déluge.","explicationEn":"27. So I revealed to him: Make a ship under My supervision and tutorage. Then, when My command to destroy them is issued and water gushes forth from the place where bread is baked, start taking a male and female from every living species onto the ship, so that they can procreate and not become extinct. Also take your family on board, except for those upon whom Allah’s decree of destruction has been passed i.e. your wife and son. Do not request Me to save and not destroy those who have wronged through disbelief; there is no doubt they shall be destroyed by drowning in the water of the flood.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023027","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-26.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-28.html"},{"numVerset":28,"texteArabe":"فَإِذَا اسْتَوَيْتَ أَنْتَ وَمَنْ مَعَكَ عَلَى الْفُلْكِ فَقُلِ الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ الَّذِي نَجَّانَا مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الظَّالِمِينَ","tradPropre":"Et lorsque tu seras installé, toi et ceux qui sont avec toi, dans l'arche, dis: «Louange à Allah qui nous a sauvés du peuple des injustes».","tradEn":"And when you have boarded the ship, you and those with you, then say, 'Praise to Allāh who has saved us from the wrongdoing people.'","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Lorsque tu embarqueras sur le bateau avec les croyants qui t’accompagnent, dis: Louange à Allah qui nous a sauvés du peuple mécréant qu’Il a anéanti.","explicationEn":"28. When you board the ship together with the believers achieving salvation, say: “All praise is for Allah Who saved us from the disbelieving people and destroyed them.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023028","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-27.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-29.html"},{"numVerset":29,"texteArabe":"وَقُلْ رَبِّ أَنْزِلْنِي مُنْزَلًا مُبَارَكًا وَأَنْتَ خَيْرُ الْمُنْزِلِينَ","tradPropre":"Et dis: «Seigneur, fais-moi débarquer d'un débarquement béni. Tu es Celui qui procure le meilleur débarquement».","tradEn":"And say, 'My Lord, let me land at a blessed landing place, and You are the best to accommodate [us].'\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Dis aussi: Ô mon Seigneur, fais-moi débarquer dans un lieu béni car Tu es Celui qui procure le meilleur débarquement.","explicationEn":"29. And say: “O my Lord! Cause me to disembark at a blessed place, for You are the best of those who cause to disembark.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023029","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-28.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-30.html"},{"numVerset":30,"texteArabe":"إِنَّ فِي ذَالِكَ لَآيَاتٍ وَإِنْ كُنَّا لَمُبْتَلِينَ","tradPropre":"Voilà bien là des signes. Nous sommes certes Celui qui éprouve.","tradEn":"Indeed in that are signs, and indeed, We are ever testing [Our servants].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Le fait que Noé et les croyants aient été sauvés et que les mécréants aient été anéantis sont les preuves claires que Nous avons le pouvoir de secourir Nos messagers et d’anéantir ceux qui les démentent. Nous avons éprouvé le peuple de Noé en le leur envoyant, afin que les croyants parmi eux se distinguent des mécréants et que les obéissants se distinguent des désobéissants.","explicationEn":"30. Indeed, in the aforementioned, i.e. saving Noah and the believers with him, and destroying the disbelievers, are great signs of My ability to help My messengers and destroy their rejecters. I had tested the people of Noah by sending him to them, so that the believers and disbelievers, the obedient and sinners become distinct.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023030","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-29.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-31.html"},{"numVerset":31,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ أَنْشَأْنَا مِنْ بَعْدِهِمْ قَرْنًا آخَرِينَ","tradPropre":"Puis, après eux, Nous avons créé d'autres générations,","tradEn":"Then We produced after them a generation of others.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Le peuple des ‘Ad, selon certains, puisqu’il vécut immédiatement après le peuple de Noé, ou celui des Thamoud, selon d’autres, puisque ce sont les Thamoud qui furent « foudroyés » comme le décrit la fin de ce récit (verset 41).","explicationUnanime":"Puis après avoir anéanti le peuple de Noé, Nous avons créé un autre peuple.","explicationEn":"31. Thereafter, I created a different generation of people after destroying the people of Noah. They were the Ād, the people of Hud (peace be upon him).","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023031","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-30.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-32.html"},{"numVerset":32,"texteArabe":"فَأَرْسَلْنَا فِيهِمْ رَسُولًا مِنْهُمْ أَنِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِنْ إِلَاهٍ غَيْرُهُ  أَفَلَا تَتَّقُونَ","tradPropre":"Nous envoyâmes parmi elles un Messager [issu] d'elles pour leur dire: «Adorez Allah. Vous n'avez pas d'autre divinité en dehors de Lui. Ne le craignez-vous pas?»","tradEn":"And We sent among them a messenger from themselves, [saying], \"Worship Allāh; you have no deity other than Him; then will you not fear Him?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous envoyâmes ensuite parmi ce peuple un messager qui les appelait à adorer Allah et qui leur dit: Adorez Allah Seul car vous n’avez pas de dieu qui mérite d’être adoré hormis Lui. Ne le craindrez-vous pas en renonçant à ce qu’Il vous a interdit et en vous conformant à Ses commandements?","explicationEn":"32. I sent to them a messenger from amongst them: Hud, who would call them towards Allah. He said to them, “O my people! Worship Allah only; you do not have any true deity except Him, may He be glorified. Will you not be mindful of Allah by fulfilling His commands and refraining from His prohibitions?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023032","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-31.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-33.html"},{"numVerset":33,"texteArabe":"وَقَالَ الْمَلَأُ مِنْ قَوْمِهِ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا وَكَذَّبُوا بِلِقَاءِ الْآخِرَةِ وَأَتْرَفْنَاهُمْ فِي الْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا مَا هَاذَا إِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِثْلُكُمْ يَأْكُلُ مِمَّا تَأْكُلُونَ مِنْهُ وَيَشْرَبُ مِمَّا تَشْرَبُونَ","tradPropre":"Les notables de son peuple qui avaient mécru et traité de mensonge la rencontre de l'au-delà, et auxquels Nous avions accordé le luxe dans la vie présente, dirent: «Celui-ci n'est qu'un être humain comme vous, mangeant de ce que vous mangez, et buvant de ce que vous buvez.","tradEn":"And the eminent among his people who disbelieved and denied the meeting of the Hereafter while We had given them luxury in the worldly life said, \"This is not but a man like yourselves. He eats of that from which you eat and drinks of what you drink.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les nobles et les chefs de ce nouveau peuple étaient mécréants, rejetaient la réalité du Jour de la Résurrection ainsi que la récompense ou la punition que les gens y recevront et étaient devenus tyranniques du fait des immenses bienfaits dont Nous les avions comblés dans le bas monde. Ces notables et chefs dirent à leurs suiveurs et aux gens du peuple: Il n’est qu’un être humain comme vous, qui mange de ce que vous mangez et boit de ce que vous buvez. Il ne vous est donc supérieur en rien pour qu’il vous soit envoyé comme messager.","explicationEn":"33. The noblemen and leaders from his people who disbelieved in Allah, rejected the Hereafter and the punishment and reward to be meted out in it, and were misled by the blessings I had granted them in the world, said to their followers and masses, “This is a human just like you are: he eats of the food you eat and drinks of the drinks you drink. He does not have any superiority over you such that he would be sent as a messenger to you!”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023033","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-32.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-34.html"},{"numVerset":34,"texteArabe":"وَلَئِنْ أَطَعْتُمْ بَشَرًا مِثْلَكُمْ إِنَّكُمْ إِذًا لَخَاسِرُونَ","tradPropre":"Si vous obéissez à un homme comme vous, vous serez alors perdants.","tradEn":"And if you should obey a man like yourselves, indeed, you would then be losers.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Si vous obéissez à un être humain comme vous, vous serez assurément perdants. Vous ne gagnerez rien à le suivre et à délaisser vos divinités.","explicationEn":"34. “And if you were to follow a human just like you, you would indeed have been deceived into leaving aside your deities and following one who has no virtue over you.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023034","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-33.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-35.html"},{"numVerset":35,"texteArabe":"أَيَعِدُكُمْ أَنَّكُمْ إِذَا مِتُّمْ وَكُنْتُمْ تُرَابًا وَعِظَامًا أَنَّكُمْ مُخْرَجُونَ","tradPropre":"Vous promet-il, quand vous serez morts, et devenus poussière et ossements, que vous serez sortis [de vos sépulcres]?","tradEn":"Does he promise you that when you have died and become dust and bones that you will be brought forth [once more]?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Cet homme qui prétend être un messager vous promet-il que lorsque vous mourrez et que vous deviendrez poussière et os poreux, vous serez sortis vivants de vos tombes? Cela est-il concevable?","explicationEn":"35. “Does this man who claims to be a messenger promise you that when you die and become dust and decomposed bones, that you shall leave your graves alive? Is this even conceivable?!”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023035","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-34.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-36.html"},{"numVerset":36,"texteArabe":"۞ هَيْهَاتَ هَيْهَاتَ لِمَا تُوعَدُونَ","tradPropre":"Loin, loin, ce qu'on vous promet!","tradEn":"How far, how far, is that which you are promised.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ce que l’on vous promet là est très loin d’être réalisable.","explicationEn":"36. The promise you are being given in being taken out of your graves alive after you have died and turned into dust and decomposed bones, is very far from reality.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023036","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-35.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-37.html"},{"numVerset":37,"texteArabe":"إِنْ هِيَ إِلَّا حَيَاتُنَا الدُّنْيَا نَمُوتُ وَنَحْيَا وَمَا نَحْنُ بِمَبْعُوثِينَ","tradPropre":"Ce n'est là que notre vie présente: nous mourons et nous vivons; et nous ne serons jamais ressuscités.","tradEn":"It [i.e., life] is not but our worldly life - we die and live, but we will not be resurrected.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"La vie ne se résume qu’à celle de ce bas monde et il n’y aura pas d’au-delà. Les vivants meurent et les morts ne reviennent pas à la vie. D’autres gens naîtront après notre mort et nous ne serons pas sortis de nos tombes pour rendre des comptes le Jour de la Résurrection.","explicationEn":"37. The only life is the life of this world, not the afterlife. The living from among us die and are not revived, whilst others are born and live. We are not going to be taken out after we have died, to be taken to account on the Day of Judgment.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023037","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-36.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-38.html"},{"numVerset":38,"texteArabe":"إِنْ هُوَ إِلَّا رَجُلٌ افْتَرَىٰ عَلَى اللَّهِ كَذِبًا وَمَا نَحْنُ لَهُ بِمُؤْمِنِينَ","tradPropre":"Ce n'est qu'un homme qui forge un mensonge contre Allah; et nous ne croirons pas en lui».","tradEn":"He is not but a man who has invented a lie about Allāh, and we will not believe him.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Celui qui prétend avoir été envoyé à vous n’est qu’un homme qui invente des mensonges sur Allah et Nous ne lui accorderons aucun crédit.","explicationEn":"38. Hud, who claims he is a messenger, has only fabricated a lie unto Allah by this claim of his; we are not going to believe him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023038","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-37.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-39.html"},{"numVerset":39,"texteArabe":"قَالَ رَبِّ انْصُرْنِي بِمَا كَذَّبُونِ","tradPropre":"Il dit: «Seigneur! Apporte-moi secours parce qu'ils me traitent de menteur».","tradEn":"He said, \"My Lord, support me because they have denied me.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Le Messager dit: Ô mon Seigneur, secours-moi contre eux et venge-moi d’eux pour m’avoir traité de menteur.","explicationEn":"39. Hud said, “O my Lord! Help me against them and pay them back for their rejection and defiance!”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023039","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-38.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-40.html"},{"numVerset":40,"texteArabe":"قَالَ عَمَّا قَلِيلٍ لَيُصْبِحُنَّ نَادِمِينَ","tradPropre":"[Allah] dit: «Oui, bientôt ils en viendront aux regrets».","tradEn":"[Allāh] said, \"After a little, they will surely become regretful.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allah lui répondit: Dans pas longtemps, ces dénégateurs seront pleins de regret pour le comportement qui est le leur aujourd’hui.","explicationEn":"40. Allah responded to him, saying, “Very soon, these people who have rejected the message you have brought to them will regret their rejection.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023040","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-39.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-41.html"},{"numVerset":41,"texteArabe":"فَأَخَذَتْهُمُ الصَّيْحَةُ بِالْحَقِّ فَجَعَلْنَاهُمْ غُثَاءً  فَبُعْدًا لِلْقَوْمِ الظَّالِمِينَ","tradPropre":"Le cri, donc, les saisit en toute justice; puis Nous les rendîmes semblables à des débris emportés par le torrent. Que disparaissent à jamais les injustes!","tradEn":"So the shriek seized them in truth, and We made them as [plant] stubble. Then away with the wrongdoing people.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils furent aussitôt surpris par un cri très strident et destructeur et ceci est le châtiment qu’ils méritaient. Je les ai alors rendus aussi inertes que l’écume. Que soient donc anéantis les peuples injustes!","explicationEn":"41. So a severe scream, accompanied by a severe wind, took them by surprise, due to their deserving the punishment owing to their stubbornness. I destroyed them, leaving them like the froth of the flood. Woe be to the transgressing nation!","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023041","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-40.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-42.html"},{"numVerset":42,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ أَنْشَأْنَا مِنْ بَعْدِهِمْ قُرُونًا آخَرِينَ","tradPropre":"Puis après eux Nous avons créé d'autres générations.","tradEn":"Then We produced after them other generations.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Puis après avoir anéanti ces gens, Nous avons créé d’autres peuples encore, à l’image du peuple de Loth, du peuple de Chu’ayb et du peuple de Yûnus.","explicationEn":"42. Then, after destroying them, I created other peoples and nations, like the nation of Lot, Shu‘ayb and Jonah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023042","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-41.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-43.html"},{"numVerset":43,"texteArabe":"مَا تَسْبِقُ مِنْ أُمَّةٍ أَجَلَهَا وَمَا يَسْتَأْخِرُونَ","tradPropre":"Nulle communauté ne peut avancer ni reculer son terme.","tradEn":"No nation will precede its time [of termination], nor will they remain [thereafter].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Aucun de ces peuples dénégateurs ne pourra avancer ni reculer le terme fixée pour son anéantissement, quels que soient les moyens auxquels il a recours.","explicationEn":"43. None of these rejecting nations will precede the time fixed for their destruction, nor will they be delayed from it, regardless of whatever means they have at their disposal.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023043","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-42.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-44.html"},{"numVerset":44,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ أَرْسَلْنَا رُسُلَنَا تَتْرَىٰ  كُلَّ مَا جَاءَ أُمَّةً رَسُولُهَا كَذَّبُوهُ  فَأَتْبَعْنَا بَعْضَهُمْ بَعْضًا وَجَعَلْنَاهُمْ أَحَادِيثَ  فَبُعْدًا لِقَوْمٍ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ","tradPropre":"Ensuite, Nous envoyâmes successivement Nos messagers. Chaque fois qu'un messager se présentait à sa communauté, ils le traitaient de menteur. Et Nous les fîmes succéder les unes aux autres [dans la destruction], et Nous en fîmes des thèmes de récits légendaires. Que disparaissent à jamais les gens qui ne croient pas!","tradEn":"Then We sent Our messengers in succession. Every time there came to a nation its messenger, they denied him, so We made them follow one another [to destruction], and We made them narrations. So away with a people who do not believe.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Plus tard, Nous avons envoyé des messagers qui ont succédé les uns aux autres et chaque fois qu’un messager s’adressait au peuple auquel Nous l’avons envoyé, il fut démenti. Nous anéantîmes alors ces peuples l’un après l’autre et il ne subsiste d’eux que les récits que les gens se transmettent à leur sujet. Que soient donc anéantis les gens qui ne croient pas à ce que leurs messagers leur rapportent de leur Seigneur.","explicationEn":"44. I then sent My messengers in succession, one after the other. Each time the Messenger came to his nation he was sent to they rejected him, so I successively destroyed them, leaving nothing except for the tales of people regarding them. So destruction be to the nation that does not believe in the message brought to it by a messenger sent to it!","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023044","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-43.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-45.html"},{"numVerset":45,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ أَرْسَلْنَا مُوسَىٰ وَأَخَاهُ هَارُونَ بِآيَاتِنَا وَسُلْطَانٍ مُبِينٍ","tradPropre":"Ensuite, Nous envoyâmes Moïse et son frère Aaron avec Nos prodiges et une preuve évidente,","tradEn":"Then We sent Moses and his brother Aaron with Our signs and a clear authority","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Puis Nous avons envoyé Moïse et son frère Aaron accompagnés de Nos neuf signes: Le bâton, la main, les sauterelles, les poux, les grenouilles, le sang, le déluge, les années de vache maigre et la pénurie de récoltes. Nous les avons également dotés d’arguments imparables.","explicationEn":"45. I then sent Moses and his brother Aaron with nine of My signs: the Staff, the Hand, locusts, lice, frogs, blood, floods, drought and shortage of produce, and with clear proof.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023045","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-44.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-46.html"},{"numVerset":46,"texteArabe":"إِلَىٰ فِرْعَوْنَ وَمَلَئِهِ فَاسْتَكْبَرُوا وَكَانُوا قَوْمًا عَالِينَ","tradPropre":"vers Pharaon et ses notables mais ceux-ci s'enflèrent d'orgueil: ils étaient des gens hautains.","tradEn":"To Pharaoh and his establishment, but they were arrogant and were a haughty people.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous les avons envoyés à Pharaon et aux nobles de son peuple mais ceux-ci se détournèrent avec orgueil et refusèrent de croire. Ils étaient assurément un peuple arrogant qui dominaient les gens par la force et l’injustice.","explicationEn":"46. I sent them both to Pharaoh and the noblemen of his people, but they displayed arrogance and did not submit to believing in them. They were a people who imposed themselves upon people by subduing and oppressing them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023046","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-45.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-47.html"},{"numVerset":47,"texteArabe":"فَقَالُوا أَنُؤْمِنُ لِبَشَرَيْنِ مِثْلِنَا وَقَوْمُهُمَا لَنَا عَابِدُونَ","tradPropre":"Ils dirent: «Croirons-nous en deux hommes comme nous dont les congénères sont nos esclaves».","tradEn":"They said, \"Should we believe two men like ourselves while their people are for us in servitude?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils répondirent ceci à l’appel de Moïse et d’Aaron: Allons-nous croire que deux humains comme nous qui ne nous surpassent en rien, nous ont été envoyés comme messagers alors que leur peuple, les Israélites, nous sont asservis?","explicationEn":"47. So they said, “Should we believe two humans like us, who have no superiority over us and their tribe (the Israelites) are submissive and obedient to us?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023047","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-46.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-48.html"},{"numVerset":48,"texteArabe":"فَكَذَّبُوهُمَا فَكَانُوا مِنَ الْمُهْلَكِينَ","tradPropre":"Ils les traitèrent [tous deux] de menteurs et ils furent donc parmi les anéantis.","tradEn":"So they denied them and were of those destroyed.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils les démentirent alors et c’est pour cette raison qu’ils furent tous noyés.","explicationEn":"48. So they rejected whatever message they brought to them from Allah. And because of their rejection, they were destroyed by drowning.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023048","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-47.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-49.html"},{"numVerset":49,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ آتَيْنَا مُوسَى الْكِتَابَ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَهْتَدُونَ","tradPropre":"Et Nous avions apporté le Livre à Moïse afin qu'ils se guident.","tradEn":"And We certainly gave Moses the Scripture that perhaps they would be guided.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons donné à Moïse la Torah dans l’espoir que grâce à elle, son peuple soit guidé vers la vérité et qu’ils mettent en pratique ses enseignements.","explicationEn":"49. Verily, I gave Moses the Torah in the hope that his people would be guided to the truth through it and implement its teachings.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023049","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-48.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-50.html"},{"numVerset":50,"texteArabe":"وَجَعَلْنَا ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ وَأُمَّهُ آيَةً وَآوَيْنَاهُمَا إِلَىٰ رَبْوَةٍ ذَاتِ قَرَارٍ وَمَعِينٍ","tradPropre":"Et Nous fîmes du fils de Marie, ainsi que de sa mère, un prodige; et Nous donnâmes à tous deux asile sur une colline bien stable et dotée d'une source.","tradEn":"And We made the son of Mary and his mother a sign and sheltered them within a high ground having level [areas] and flowing water.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons fait de Jésus et de sa mère Marie, un signe de Notre pouvoir puisque Marie fut enceinte de Jésus alors qu’elle n’avait pas eu de rapports intimes avec un homme. Nous les avons installés dans un lieu surélevé et plat où il fait bon vivre et où l’eau coule à flot.","explicationEn":"50. I also made Jesus and his mother Mary signs indicating My capability; she conceived him without a father. I granted them shelter in an elevated place on earth, an even, habitable place which had fresh flowing water.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023050","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-49.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-51.html"},{"numVerset":51,"texteArabe":"يَا أَيُّهَا الرُّسُلُ كُلُوا مِنَ الطَّيِّبَاتِ وَاعْمَلُوا صَالِحًا  إِنِّي بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ عَلِيمٌ","tradPropre":"O Messagers! Mangez de ce qui est permis et agréable et faites du bien. Car Je sais parfaitement ce que vous faites.","tradEn":"[Allāh said], \"O messengers, eat from the good foods and work righteousness. Indeed I, of what you do, am Knowing.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô messagers, mangez des bonnes nourritures que Je vous ai déclarées licites et accomplissez de bonnes œuvres conformes aux préceptes de la religion car Je sais le mieux ce que vous faites et rien ne M’échappe.","explicationEn":"51. O Messengers! Eat from the appealing food that I have made lawful for you, and perform good deeds in accordance to the laws of Allah. Indeed, I am ever aware of every action of yours; none of your actions are hidden from Me.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023051","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-50.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-52.html"},{"numVerset":52,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّ هَاذِهِ أُمَّتُكُمْ أُمَّةً وَاحِدَةً وَأَنَا رَبُّكُمْ فَاتَّقُونِ","tradPropre":"Cette communauté, la vôtre, est une seule communauté, tandis que Je suis votre Seigneur. Craignez-Moi donc».","tradEn":"And indeed this, your religion, is one religion, and I am your Lord, so fear Me.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô messagers, votre religion est une, c’est l’Islam, et Je suis votre Seul Seigneur. Craignez-moi donc en vous conformant à Mes commandements et en renonçant à ce que je vous ai défendu.","explicationEn":"52. O Messengers! Indeed, your creed is one creed: it is Islam. And I am your Lord, you do not have a Lord other than Me, so be mindful of Me by fulfilling My commands and refraining from My prohibitions.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023052","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-51.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-53.html"},{"numVerset":53,"texteArabe":"فَتَقَطَّعُوا أَمْرَهُمْ بَيْنَهُمْ زُبُرًا  كُلُّ حِزْبٍ بِمَا لَدَيْهِمْ فَرِحُونَ","tradPropre":"Mais ils se sont divisés en sectes, chaque secte exultant de ce qu'elle détenait.","tradEn":"But they [i.e., the people] divided their religion among them into portions [i.e., sects] - each faction, in what it has, rejoicing.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Ceux qui ensuite se sont réclamés de ces prophètes tout en se détournant de leur voie.","explicationUnanime":"Seulement, leurs disciples se sont divisés en sectes. Chacune de ces sectes revendique qu’elle pratique la religion agréée par Allah et n’accorde aucune importance à ce que pratiquent les autres comme religion","explicationEn":"53. After they passed away, their followers were divided in religion and became sects and groups, with each group conceited in believing that whatever it believed in was the true acceptable religion according to Allah, disregarding the views of anyone else.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023053","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-52.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-54.html"},{"numVerset":54,"texteArabe":"فَذَرْهُمْ فِي غَمْرَتِهِمْ حَتَّىٰ حِينٍ","tradPropre":"Laisse-les dans leur égarement pour un certain temps.","tradEn":"So leave them in their confusion for a time.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, laisse-les se débattre dans leur ignorance et dans leur indécision jusqu’à ce que le châtiment s’abatte sur eux.","explicationEn":"54. O Messenger! Leave them in the ignorance and confusion they are in, until the punishment descends upon them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023054","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-53.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-55.html"},{"numVerset":55,"texteArabe":"أَيَحْسَبُونَ أَنَّمَا نُمِدُّهُمْ بِهِ مِنْ مَالٍ وَبَنِينَ","tradPropre":"Pensent-ils que ce que Nous leur accordons, en biens et en enfants,","tradEn":"Do they think that what We extend to them of wealth and children","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les adeptes de ces sectes qui sont satisfaits de leur pratique religieuse, pensent-ils que les richesses et la descendance que Nous leur accordons dans le bas monde est une avance sur la récompense qu’ils méritent? Il n’en est pas du tout ainsi. Nous ne leur faisons ces dons que pour les mener graduellement à leur perte mais ils sont inconscients de cela.","explicationEn":"56. Do these self-conceited groups think that whatever wealth and offspring we bestow them with in the world, is a prelude of good they deserve? It is not as they think; I am only giving it to them as respite, gradually leading them into destruction, but they do not realise it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023055","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-54.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-56.html"},{"numVerset":56,"texteArabe":"نُسَارِعُ لَهُمْ فِي الْخَيْرَاتِ  بَلْ لَا يَشْعُرُونَ","tradPropre":"[soit une avance] que Nous Nous empressons de leur faire sur les biens [de la vie future]? Au contraire, ils n'en sont pas conscients.","tradEn":"Is [because] We hasten for them good things? Rather, they do not perceive.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les adeptes de ces sectes qui sont satisfaits de leur pratique religieuse, pensent-ils que les richesses et la descendance que Nous leur accordons dans le bas monde est une avance sur la récompense qu’ils méritent? Il n’en est pas du tout ainsi. Nous ne leur faisons ces dons que pour les mener graduellement à leur perte mais ils sont inconscients de cela.","explicationEn":"56. Do these self-conceited groups think that whatever wealth and offspring we bestow them with in the world, is a prelude of good they deserve? It is not as they think; I am only giving it to them as respite, gradually leading them into destruction, but they do not realise it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023056","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-55.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-57.html"},{"numVerset":57,"texteArabe":"إِنَّ الَّذِينَ هُمْ مِنْ خَشْيَةِ رَبِّهِمْ مُشْفِقُونَ","tradPropre":"Ceux qui, de la crainte de leur Seigneur, sont pénétrés,","tradEn":"Indeed, they who are apprehensive from fear of their Lord","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ceux qui, en plus d’être croyants et bienfaisants, redoutent leur Seigneur,","explicationEn":"57. Indeed, those who, despite their belief and good, are fearful of their Lord.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023057","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-56.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-58.html"},{"numVerset":58,"texteArabe":"وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ بِآيَاتِ رَبِّهِمْ يُؤْمِنُونَ","tradPropre":"qui croient aux versets de leur Seigneur,","tradEn":"And they who believe in the signs of their Lord","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"croient aux versets de Son Livre.","explicationEn":"58. And those who believe in the universal and religious signs of their Lord.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023058","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-57.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-59.html"},{"numVerset":59,"texteArabe":"وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ بِرَبِّهِمْ لَا يُشْرِكُونَ","tradPropre":"qui n'associent rien à leur Seigneur,","tradEn":"And they who do not associate anything with their Lord","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"adorent leur Seigneur Seul et ne Lui associent rien.","explicationEn":"59. And those who proclaim the oneness of their Lord, without ascribing anything to Him as partner.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023059","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-58.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-60.html"},{"numVerset":60,"texteArabe":"وَالَّذِينَ يُؤْتُونَ مَا آتَوْا وَقُلُوبُهُمْ وَجِلَةٌ أَنَّهُمْ إِلَىٰ رَبِّهِمْ رَاجِعُونَ","tradPropre":"qui donnent ce qu'ils donnent, tandis que leurs cœurs sont pleins de crainte [à la pensée] qu'ils doivent retourner à leur Seigneur.","tradEn":"And they who give what they give while their hearts are fearful because they will be returning to their Lord -","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils accomplissent de bonnes œuvres avec assiduité et se rapprochent d’Allah en accomplissant ces œuvres tout en craignant qu’Allah n’acceptera pas leurs dépenses et leur charité lorsqu’ils retourneront auprès de Lui le Jour de la Résurrection.","explicationEn":"60. Those who strive in doing righteous deeds and draw closer to Allah through them, whilst fearing that He may not accept their spending in His path, or good deeds when they return to Him on the Day of Judgment.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023060","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-59.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-61.html"},{"numVerset":61,"texteArabe":"أُولَائِكَ يُسَارِعُونَ فِي الْخَيْرَاتِ وَهُمْ لَهَا سَابِقُونَ","tradPropre":"Ceux-là se précipitent vers les bonnes actions et sont les premiers à les accomplir.","tradEn":"It is those who hasten to good deeds, and they outstrip [others] therein.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ceux qui détiennent ces nobles qualités s’empressent d’accomplir de bonnes œuvres et y devancent tout le monde.","explicationEn":"61. Those possessing these lofty characteristics hasten towards good deeds, and beat others in performing them. That is why they surpass everyone else.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023061","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-60.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-62.html"},{"numVerset":62,"texteArabe":"وَلَا نُكَلِّفُ نَفْسًا إِلَّا وُسْعَهَا  وَلَدَيْنَا كِتَابٌ يَنْطِقُ بِالْحَقِّ  وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُونَ","tradPropre":"Nous n'imposons à personne que selon sa capacité. Et auprès de Nous existe un Livre qui dit la vérité, et ils ne seront pas lésés.","tradEn":"And We charge no soul except [with that within] its capacity, and with Us is a record which speaks with truth; and they will not be wronged.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Le registre des œuvres où tous les actes et toutes les paroles sont consignés, sans que rien n’en soit retranché ou n’y soit ajouté, expliquent nombre d’exégètes. Selon d’autres, il s’agirait du Livre archétype se trouvant auprès d’Allah.","explicationUnanime":"Nous ne chargeons une âme que de ce qu’elle peut supporter et Nous détenons un Livre où Nous consignons les œuvres de chacun. Ce Livre dit la vérité et on ne diminuera à personne injustement de ses bonnes œuvres ni ne lui rajoutera indûment des mauvaises.","explicationEn":"62. I do not burden any soul except with whatever actions are within its capability. I have a book in which I have recorded all the deeds of every doer; it shows the undisputable truth. The people will not be wronged by having their good deeds decreased or evil deeds increased.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023062","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-61.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-63.html"},{"numVerset":63,"texteArabe":"بَلْ قُلُوبُهُمْ فِي غَمْرَةٍ مِنْ هَاذَا وَلَهُمْ أَعْمَالٌ مِنْ دُونِ ذَالِكَ هُمْ لَهَا عَامِلُونَ","tradPropre":"Mais leurs cœurs restent dans l'ignorance à l'égard de cela [le Coran]. [En outre] ils ont d'autres actes (vils) qu'ils accomplissent,","tradEn":"But their hearts are covered with confusion over this, and they have [evil] deeds besides that [i.e., disbelief] which they are doing,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ce sont plutôt les cœurs des mécréants qui sont inattentifs à ce Livre qui dit la vérité ainsi qu’au Livre que Nous leur avons révélé. Par ailleurs, ils commettent d’autres péchés moins graves que leur mécréance.","explicationEn":"63. Rather, the hearts of the disbelievers are neglectful of this book that contains the truth, and of the book that was revealed to them. They also commit evil actions other than the disbelief that they are insistent on.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023063","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-62.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-64.html"},{"numVerset":64,"texteArabe":"حَتَّىٰ إِذَا أَخَذْنَا مُتْرَفِيهِمْ بِالْعَذَابِ إِذَا هُمْ يَجْأَرُونَ","tradPropre":"jusqu'à ce que par le châtiment Nous saisissions les plus aisés parmi eux et voilà qu'ils crient au secours.","tradEn":"Until when We seize their affluent ones with punishment, at once they are crying [to Allāh] for help.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il en sera ainsi jusqu’à ce que Nous châtiions le Jour de la Résurrection les plus aisés parmi eux dans le bas monde et ils hurleront afin qu’on les secoure.","explicationEn":"64. Until when I punish those among them who lived in luxury in the world with the punishment on the Day of Judgment, they shall raise their voices calling out for help.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023064","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-63.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-65.html"},{"numVerset":65,"texteArabe":"لَا تَجْأَرُوا الْيَوْمَ  إِنَّكُمْ مِنَّا لَا تُنْصَرُونَ","tradPropre":"«Ne criez pas aujourd'hui. Nul ne vous protègera contre Nous.","tradEn":"Do not cry out today. Indeed, by Us you will not be helped.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"On leur dira, afin de couper court à leur espoir qu’Allah leur fasse miséricorde: Ne criez pas et n’implorez aucun secours durant ce Jour, personne n’éloignera de vous le châtiment d’Allah.","explicationEn":"65. It will be said to them, depriving them of all hope in the mercy of Allah, “Do not scream and do not call for help today! There is no helper for you today who can help you against the punishment of Allah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023065","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-64.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-66.html"},{"numVerset":66,"texteArabe":"قَدْ كَانَتْ آيَاتِي تُتْلَىٰ عَلَيْكُمْ فَكُنْتُمْ عَلَىٰ أَعْقَابِكُمْ تَنْكِصُونَ","tradPropre":"Mes versets vous étaient récités auparavant; mais vous vous [en] détourniez,","tradEn":"My verses had already been recited to you, but you were turning back on your heels","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les versets du Livre d’Allah vous étaient récités dans le bas monde mais vous vous en détourniez par aversion.","explicationEn":"66. Verily, the verses of Allah would be recited to you in the world, but you would turn away from them when you heard them, in hatred for them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023066","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-65.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-67.html"},{"numVerset":67,"texteArabe":"مُسْتَكْبِرِينَ بِهِ سَامِرًا تَهْجُرُونَ","tradPropre":"s'enflant d'orgueil, et vous les dénigriez au cours de vos veillées».","tradEn":"In arrogance regarding it, conversing by night, speaking evil.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Autre sens : lorsque Mes versets vous étaient récités, vous vous en détourniez fièrement, les reniant lors de vos veillées.","explicationUnanime":"C’était votre dédain des gens découlant de votre sentiment de supériorité d’être les habitants du Sanctuaire. Or vous n’êtes pas les habitants du Sanctuaire car les authentiques habitants du Sanctuaire sont pieux. De plus, vous veillez autour de ce même Sanctuaire en proférant des paroles exécrables, ce qui signifie que vous ne le respectez pas.","explicationEn":"67. You did that displaying arrogance over the people, because you thought you were the people of the sanctuary while you were not; the true people of the sanctuary are the Mindful. You also talked ill of it by night and would not deem it sacred.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023067","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-66.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-68.html"},{"numVerset":68,"texteArabe":"أَفَلَمْ يَدَّبَّرُوا الْقَوْلَ أَمْ جَاءَهُمْ مَا لَمْ يَأْتِ آبَاءَهُمُ الْأَوَّلِينَ","tradPropre":"Ne méditent-ils donc pas sur la parole (le Coran)? Ou est-ce que leur est venu ce qui n'est jamais venu à leurs premiers ancêtres?","tradEn":"Then have they not reflected over the word [i.e., the Qur’ān], or has there come to them that which had not come to their forefathers?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ces polythéistes ne méditent-ils pas les versets qu’Allah a révélés pour finir par y croire? Ou alors, leur rejet et leur démenti s’explique-t-il par le fait qu’on leur présente un message différent de celui qui fut présenté à leurs ancêtres?","explicationEn":"68. Will these idolaters not ponder over the Qur’ān Allah has revealed, bring faith in it and implement its teachings? Or is it that something has come to them which did not come to their predecessors, so they turned away from it and rejected it?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023068","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-67.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-69.html"},{"numVerset":69,"texteArabe":"أَمْ لَمْ يَعْرِفُوا رَسُولَهُمْ فَهُمْ لَهُ مُنْكِرُونَ","tradPropre":"Ou n'ont-ils pas connu leur Messager, au point de le renier?","tradEn":"Or did they not know their Messenger, so they are toward him disacknowledging?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ou alors, n’ont-ils pas reconnu Muħammad qu’Allah leur a envoyé et l’ont renié? Pourtant, ils le connaissaient tout comme ils connaissaient sa véracité et sa loyauté.","explicationEn":"69. Or is it that they do not recognise Muhammad peace be upon him whom Allah has sent to them, and so they reject him? Verily, they recognise him, his truthfulness and his honesty.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023069","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-68.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-70.html"},{"numVerset":70,"texteArabe":"أَمْ يَقُولُونَ بِهِ جِنَّةٌ  بَلْ جَاءَهُمْ بِالْحَقِّ وَأَكْثَرُهُمْ لِلْحَقِّ كَارِهُونَ","tradPropre":"Ou diront-ils: «Il est fou?» Au contraire, c'est la vérité qu'il leur a apportée. Et la plupart d'entre eux dédaignent la vérité.","tradEn":"Or do they say, \"In him is madness\"? Rather, he brought them the truth, but most of them, to the truth, are averse.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils disent plutôt de lui qu’il est fou. Ils mentent lorsqu’ils prétendent cela. Il leur a plutôt apporté la vérité indubitable de la part d’Allah, mais la plupart d’entre eux haïssent la vérité, par envie et par fidélité obstinée à leur fausseté.","explicationEn":"70. Rather, do they say, “He is insane!”? Surely, they have lied. Rather, the truth has come to them, undisputably from Allah. The majority of them dislike the truth, hating it due to the jealousy within themselves and fanaticism over their falsehood.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023070","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-69.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-71.html"},{"numVerset":71,"texteArabe":"وَلَوِ اتَّبَعَ الْحَقُّ أَهْوَاءَهُمْ لَفَسَدَتِ السَّمَاوَاتُ وَالْأَرْضُ وَمَنْ فِيهِنَّ  بَلْ أَتَيْنَاهُمْ بِذِكْرِهِمْ فَهُمْ عَنْ ذِكْرِهِمْ مُعْرِضُونَ","tradPropre":"Si la vérité était conforme à leurs passions, les cieux et la terre et ceux qui s'y trouvent seraient, certes, corrompus. Au contraire, Nous leur avons donné leur rappel. Mais ils s'en détournent.","tradEn":"But if the Truth [i.e., Allāh] had followed their inclinations, the heavens and the earth and whoever is in them would have been ruined. Rather, We have brought them their message, but they, from their message, are turning away.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Si Allah avait géré le monde selon ce que dictent leurs passions, les Cieux et la Terre ainsi que leurs habitants seraient tous corrompus. En effet, ces gens ignorent les conséquences des actes que leur dictent leurs passions.","explicationEn":"71. If Allah was to have let matters run and arrange them in accordance to their desires, the heavens, earth and all their inhabitants would fall into ruin due to their ignorance of the outcome of matters, and their inability to differentiate between good and bad plans.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023071","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-70.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-72.html"},{"numVerset":72,"texteArabe":"أَمْ تَسْأَلُهُمْ خَرْجًا فَخَرَاجُ رَبِّكَ خَيْرٌ  وَهُوَ خَيْرُ الرَّازِقِينَ","tradPropre":"Ou leur demandes-tu une rétribution? Mais la rétribution de ton Seigneur est meilleure. Et c'est Lui, le Meilleur des pourvoyeurs.","tradEn":"Or do you, [O Muḥammad], ask them for payment? But the reward of your Lord is best, and He is the best of providers.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, as-tu demandé à ces gens une contrepartie pour ce que tu leur apportes? Est-ce pour cette raison qu’ils s’opposent à ta prédication? Tu n’as certainement pas fait une telle demande car la récompense de ton Seigneur est meilleure que la leur et Il est, exalté soit-Il, le meilleur des pourvoyeurs.","explicationEn":"72. O Messenger! Have you asked for a fee from these people for what you brought to them, which has made them reject your call? You have not done as such; the reward of your Lord is far better than the reward any of these people can give. He, may He be glorified, is the best of providers.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023072","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-71.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-73.html"},{"numVerset":73,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّكَ لَتَدْعُوهُمْ إِلَىٰ صِرَاطٍ مُسْتَقِيمٍ","tradPropre":"Et tu les appelles, certes, vers le droit chemin.","tradEn":"And indeed, you invite them to a straight path.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, tu appelles assurément ces gens-là et d’autres encore, à emprunter le droit chemin qui ne comporte aucune tortuosité: il s’agit de l’Islam.","explicationEn":"73. O Messenger! Indeed, you call these people and others towards a straight path which has no deviation: it is the path of Islam.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023073","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-72.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-74.html"},{"numVerset":74,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّ الَّذِينَ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ بِالْآخِرَةِ عَنِ الصِّرَاطِ لَنَاكِبُونَ","tradPropre":"Or, ceux qui ne croient pas à l'au-delà sont bien écartés de ce chemin.","tradEn":"But indeed, those who do not believe in the Hereafter are deviating from the path.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ceux qui ne croient pas à l’au-delà et à tout ce qui s’y produira, à savoir la Rétribution, la punition et la récompense, ceux-là dévient du chemin de l’Islam et s’engouffrent dans une voie tortueuse qui mène au Feu.","explicationEn":"74. And indeed those who do not believe in the Hearafter; accountability, punishment and reward, incline towards other paths which lead to the hellfire.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023074","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-73.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-75.html"},{"numVerset":75,"texteArabe":"۞ وَلَوْ رَحِمْنَاهُمْ وَكَشَفْنَا مَا بِهِمْ مِنْ ضُرٍّ لَلَجُّوا فِي طُغْيَانِهِمْ يَعْمَهُونَ","tradPropre":"Si Nous leur faisions miséricorde et écartions d'eux le mal, ils persisteraient certainement dans leur transgression, confus et hésitants.","tradEn":"And even if We gave them mercy and removed what was upon them of affliction, they would persist in their transgression, wandering blindly.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Si Nous leur avions fait miséricorde et avions éloigné d’eux la sécheresse et la faim, ils se seraient encore plus égarés de la vérité et s’y seraient débattus plus profondément.","explicationEn":"75. If I were to have mercy on them and lift their famine and hunger, they would continue being misguided from the truth, being confused and stumbling.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023075","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-74.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-76.html"},{"numVerset":76,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ أَخَذْنَاهُمْ بِالْعَذَابِ فَمَا اسْتَكَانُوا لِرَبِّهِمْ وَمَا يَتَضَرَّعُونَ","tradPropre":"Nous les avons certes saisis du châtiment, mais ils ne se sont pas soumis à leur Seigneur; de même qu'ils ne [Le] supplient point,","tradEn":"And We had gripped them with suffering [as a warning], but they did not yield to their Lord, nor did they humbly supplicate, [and will continue thus]","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous les avons éprouvés par une multitude de malheurs mais ils refusèrent malgré cela de se soumettre à Lui. Ils ne l’implorèrent pas non plus avec humilité afin qu’Il mette fin à ces malheurs.","explicationEn":"76. I tested them through different afflictions, but neither did they humble before their Lord or submit to Him nor did they pray to Him submissively so that He lifts the afflictions from them when they befall.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023076","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-75.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-77.html"},{"numVerset":77,"texteArabe":"حَتَّىٰ إِذَا فَتَحْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ بَابًا ذَا عَذَابٍ شَدِيدٍ إِذَا هُمْ فِيهِ مُبْلِسُونَ","tradPropre":"jusqu'au jour où Nous ouvrirons sur eux une porte au dur châtiment, et voilà qu'ils en seront désespérés.","tradEn":"Until when We have opened before them a door of severe punishment, immediately they will be therein in despair.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils persistent ainsi jusqu’à ce que Nous leur montrions le châtiment terrible qu’ils subiront et alors, ils désespèreront de tout dénouement heureux.","explicationEn":"77. Until when I opened a door of severe punishment on them, they became hopeless of every ease and good.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023077","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-76.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-78.html"},{"numVerset":78,"texteArabe":"وَهُوَ الَّذِي أَنْشَأَ لَكُمُ السَّمْعَ وَالْأَبْصَارَ وَالْأَفْئِدَةَ  قَلِيلًا مَا تَشْكُرُونَ","tradPropre":"Et c'est Lui qui a créé pour vous l'ouïe, les yeux et les cœurs. Mais vous êtes rarement reconnaissants.","tradEn":"And it is He who produced for you hearing and vision and hearts [i.e., intellect]; little are you grateful.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô vous qui rejetez la réalité de la Ressuscitation, c’est Allah qui a créé en vous l’ouïe afin que vous puissiez entendre, la vue afin que vous puissiez voir et le cœur afin que vous puissiez comprendre. Mais malgré cela, vous ne Lui êtes que rarement reconnaissants pour ces dons.","explicationEn":"78. O deniers of the resurrection, Allah is the One Who created for you hearing to listen with, vision to see with, and hearts to ponder with, but despite that, you do not thank Him for these favours except a little.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023078","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-77.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-79.html"},{"numVerset":79,"texteArabe":"وَهُوَ الَّذِي ذَرَأَكُمْ فِي الْأَرْضِ وَإِلَيْهِ تُحْشَرُونَ","tradPropre":"C'est Lui qui vous a répandus sur la terre, et c'est vers Lui que vous serez rassemblés.","tradEn":"And it is He who has multiplied you throughout the earth, and to Him you will be gathered.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô gens, c’est Lui qui vous a créés sur Terre et c’est vers Lui Seul que vous retournerez le Jour de la Résurrection. Il vous rassemblera alors afin de vous demander des comptes et vous rétribuer","explicationEn":"79. O people, it is He Who created you on earth, and to Him alone you will be raised for reckoning and reward on the Day of Judgment.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023079","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-78.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-80.html"},{"numVerset":80,"texteArabe":"وَهُوَ الَّذِي يُحْيِي وَيُمِيتُ وَلَهُ اخْتِلَافُ اللَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ  أَفَلَا تَعْقِلُونَ","tradPropre":"Et c'est Lui qui donne la vie et qui donne la mort; et l'alternance de la nuit et du jour dépend de Lui. Ne raisonnerez-vous donc pas?","tradEn":"And it is He who gives life and causes death, and His is the alternation of the night and the day. Then will you not reason?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"C’est Lui Seul qui fait vivre et qui fait mourir. Personne d’autre que Lui ne fait vivre ou mourir. C’est à Lui Seul que revient la détermination de l’alternance de la nuit et du jour et en fixe la luminosité et la longueur. N’êtes-vous pas conscients de Son pouvoir et du fait qu’Il est le Seul à créer et à gérer Sa création?","explicationEn":"80. And it is He alone Who gives life; there is nobody who gives life besides Him. And it is He alone Who gives death; there is nobody who gives death besides Him. To Him alone belongs fixing the difference of night and day, in terms of darkness and light, and length and shortness. Do you not understand His power and His being alone in creating and managing?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023080","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-79.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-81.html"},{"numVerset":81,"texteArabe":"بَلْ قَالُوا مِثْلَ مَا قَالَ الْأَوَّلُونَ","tradPropre":"Ils ont plutôt tenu les mêmes propos que les anciens.","tradEn":"Rather, they say like what the former peoples said.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils profèrent plutôt les mêmes paroles de mécréance que leurs ancêtres.","explicationEn":"81. But they said what their forefathers and predecessors in disbelief said.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023081","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-80.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-82.html"},{"numVerset":82,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا أَإِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا وَعِظَامًا أَإِنَّا لَمَبْعُوثُونَ","tradPropre":"Ils ont dit: «lorsque nous serons morts et que nous serons poussière et ossements, serons-nous vraiment ressuscités?","tradEn":"They said, \"When we have died and become dust and bones, are we indeed to be resurrected?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils dirent sur un ton désapprobateur: Seront-nous ressuscités pour rendre des comptes après que nous soyons devenus de la poussière et que nos os se soient dégradés?","explicationEn":"82. They said, unbelievingly and denyingly: “When we die and turn into dust and decomposed bones, will we be raised alive to be reckoned?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023082","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-81.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-83.html"},{"numVerset":83,"texteArabe":"لَقَدْ وُعِدْنَا نَحْنُ وَآبَاؤُنَا هَاذَا مِنْ قَبْلُ إِنْ هَاذَا إِلَّا أَسَاطِيرُ الْأَوَّلِينَ","tradPropre":"On nous a promis cela, ainsi qu'à nos ancêtres auparavant; ce ne sont que de vieilles sornettes».","tradEn":"We have been promised this, we and our forefathers, before; this is not but legends of the former peoples.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"On nous a fait la promesse de nous ressusciter après notre mort et cette promesse a aussi été faite à nos ancêtres auparavant. Or nous ne l’avons pas vue se réaliser. Cela signifie que ce n’est qu’un mensonge hérité des anciens.","explicationEn":"83. We were promised this, i.e. resurrection after death, and so were our predecessors promised this before, but we did not see this promise fulfilled. These are only the false tales and lies of the previous people”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023083","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-82.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-84.html"},{"numVerset":84,"texteArabe":"قُلْ لِمَنِ الْأَرْضُ وَمَنْ فِيهَا إِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ","tradPropre":"Dis: «A qui appartient la terre et ceux qui y sont? si vous savez».","tradEn":"Say, [O Muḥammad], \"To whom belongs the earth and whoever is in it, if you should know?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, dis à ces mécréants qui rejettent la réalité de la Ressuscitation: A qui appartient cette Terre et ceux qui s’y trouvent si vous le savez?","explicationEn":"84. O Messenger, say to these disbelievers who deny the resurrection: “Who does this earth and those on it belong to, if you have any knowledge?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023084","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-83.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-85.html"},{"numVerset":85,"texteArabe":"سَيَقُولُونَ لِلَّهِ  قُلْ أَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُونَ","tradPropre":"Ils diront: «A Allah». Dis: «Ne vous souvenez-vous donc pas?»","tradEn":"They will say, \"To Allāh.\" Say, \"Then will you not remember?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils répondront: La Terre et tous ceux qu’elle contient appartiennent à Allah. Dis-leur alors: Ne vous rappelez-vous pas que Celui qui possède la Terre et tous ceux qu’elle contient, a le pouvoir de vous faire revivre après votre mort?","explicationEn":"85. They will say: “The earth and all upon it belong to Allah”, so say to them: “Do you not then remember that the One to Whom belong the earth and all upon it has the power to restore you to life after you die?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023085","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-84.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-86.html"},{"numVerset":86,"texteArabe":"قُلْ مَنْ رَبُّ السَّمَاوَاتِ السَّبْعِ وَرَبُّ الْعَرْشِ الْعَظِيمِ","tradPropre":"Dis: «Qui est le Seigneur des sept cieux et le Seigneur du Trône sublime?»","tradEn":"Say, \"Who is Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the Great Throne?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ensuite, dis-leur: Qui est le Seigneur des Sept Cieux et qui est le Seigneur du Trône Suprême au-dessus duquel ne se trouve aucune créature?","explicationEn":"86. Say to them: “Who is the Lord of the seven heavens and who is the Lord of the Great Throne, besides which there is no bigger creation?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023086","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-85.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-87.html"},{"numVerset":87,"texteArabe":"سَيَقُولُونَ لِلَّهِ  قُلْ أَفَلَا تَتَّقُونَ","tradPropre":"Ils diront: [ils appartiennent] «A Allah». Dis: «Ne craignez-vous donc pas?»","tradEn":"They will say, \"[They belong] to Allāh.\" Say, \"Then will you not fear Him?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils répondront: Les Sept Cieux et le Trône Suprême sont les propriétés d’Allah. Dis-leur ensuite: Ne craindrez-vous pas Allah en vous conformant à Ses commandements et en renonçant à ce qu’Il vous a défendu afin d’échapper à Son châtiment?","explicationEn":"87. They will say: “The seven heavens and the Great Throne are the property of Allah”, so say to them: “Will you not then by mindful of Allah by carrying out His orders and refraining from His prohibitions, so that you are saved from His punishment?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023087","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-86.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-88.html"},{"numVerset":88,"texteArabe":"قُلْ مَنْ بِيَدِهِ مَلَكُوتُ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ وَهُوَ يُجِيرُ وَلَا يُجَارُ عَلَيْهِ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ","tradPropre":"Dis: «Qui détient dans sa main la royauté absolue de toute chose, et qui protège et n'a pas besoin d'être protégé? [Dites], si vous le savez!»","tradEn":"Say, \"In whose hand is the realm of all things - and He protects while none can protect against Him - if you should know?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Dis-leur: Qui est le Propriétaire de toute chose sans exception, Celui qui secourt ceux qu’Il veut parmi Ses serviteurs et dont personne ne peut se soustraire à Son châtiment si vous le savez?","explicationEn":"88. Say to them: “Who is the One in whose hand is the realm of everything, with nothing escaping His realm, Who helps whom He wants from His servants, with nobody being able to protect whom He intends bad for so as to remove punishment from Him, if you have any knowledge?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023088","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-87.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-89.html"},{"numVerset":89,"texteArabe":"سَيَقُولُونَ لِلَّهِ  قُلْ فَأَنَّىٰ تُسْحَرُونَ","tradPropre":"Ils diront: «Allah». Dis: «Comment donc se fait-il que vous soyez ensorcelés?» [au point de ne pas croire en Lui].","tradEn":"They will say, \"[All belongs] to Allāh.\" Say, \"Then how are you deluded?\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Pour associer d’autres divinités à Allah, alors que vous reconnaissez qu’Il est le Maître absolu de l’univers.","explicationUnanime":"Ils répondront: A Lui revient la possession de toute chose, exalté soit-Il. Dis-leur alors: Comment perdez-vous la raison et adorez-vous d’autres divinités que Lui après cet aveu?","explicationEn":"89. They will say: “In Allah's hands belong all things”, so say to them: “So how do you lose your senses and worship others besides Him, whilst you profess to that?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023089","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-88.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-90.html"},{"numVerset":90,"texteArabe":"بَلْ أَتَيْنَاهُمْ بِالْحَقِّ وَإِنَّهُمْ لَكَاذِبُونَ","tradPropre":"Nous leur avons plutôt apporté la vérité et ils sont assurément des menteurs.","tradEn":"Rather, We have brought them the truth, and indeed they are liars.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il n’en est pas comme ils le prétendent. Nous leur avons plutôt apporté la vérité indubitable et ils mentent lorsqu’ils attribuent à Allah un associé et une progéniture. Qu’Il soit grandement élevé au-dessus de ce qu’ils disent!","explicationEn":"90. The matter is not as they claim. But rather, I have brought them the truth in which there is no doubt. They are lying in their claiming a partner and child for Allah. Allah is far above what they say.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023090","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-89.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-91.html"},{"numVerset":91,"texteArabe":"مَا اتَّخَذَ اللَّهُ مِنْ وَلَدٍ وَمَا كَانَ مَعَهُ مِنْ إِلَاهٍ  إِذًا لَذَهَبَ كُلُّ إِلَاهٍ بِمَا خَلَقَ وَلَعَلَا بَعْضُهُمْ عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍ  سُبْحَانَ اللَّهِ عَمَّا يَصِفُونَ","tradPropre":"Allah ne S'est point attribué d'enfant et il n'existe point de divinité avec Lui; sinon, chaque divinité s'en irait avec ce qu'elle a créé, et certaines seraient supérieures aux autres. (Gloire et pureté) à Allah! Il est Supérieur à tout ce qu'ils décrivent.","tradEn":"Allāh has not taken any son, nor has there ever been with Him any deity. [If there had been], then each deity would have taken what it created, and some of them would have [sought to] overcome others. Exalted is Allāh above what they describe [concerning Him].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allah ne s’est pas donné de progéniture comme le prétendent les mécréants et il n’existe pas de dieu méritant d’être adoré en dehors de Lui. S’il existait d’autres dieux que Lui, chacun de ces dieux s’en irait avec la part de la Création dont il est l’auteur et certains en domineraient d’autres, ce qui mènerait l’Univers à la ruine. Or la réalité est toute autre et démontre que le Seul Dieu méritant d’être adoré est Allah, qu’Il soit purifié et sanctifié contre ce que Lui attribuent les polythéistes comme progéniture et associés.","explicationEn":"91. Allah has not taken a child as the disbelievers claim, nor is there any true deity alongside Him. If there were to be any true deity alongside Him, every deity would take his share of the creation he made and they would dominate one another, causing the order of the Universe to become corrupt. The reality is that none of this has occurred, proving that the true deity is Allah alone. He is pure and holy of what the idolaters describe Him with, namely partners and children which are unbefitting for Him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023091","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-90.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-92.html"},{"numVerset":92,"texteArabe":"عَالِمِ الْغَيْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ فَتَعَالَىٰ عَمَّا يُشْرِكُونَ","tradPropre":"[Il est] Connaisseur de toute chose visible et invisible! Il est bien au-dessus de ce qu'ils [Lui] associent!","tradEn":"[He is] Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, so high is He above what they associate [with Him].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il connaît toute chose inconnue à Ses créatures et connaît également tout ce qui est perceptible par la vue et par les sens. Rien ne Lui échappe de tout cela. Il est donc exclu qu’il ait un associé.","explicationEn":"92. He is Knowing of everything hidden from His creation and Knowing of everything which can be seen and perceived through the senses. None of this is hidden from Him. Allah is above having a partner.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023092","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-91.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-93.html"},{"numVerset":93,"texteArabe":"قُلْ رَبِّ إِمَّا تُرِيَنِّي مَا يُوعَدُونَ","tradPropre":"Dis: «Seigneur, si jamais Tu me montres ce qui leur est promis;","tradEn":"Say, [O Muḥammad], \"My Lord, if You should show me that which they are promised,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, dis: Ô mon Seigneur, lorsque Tu me montreras le châtiment que Tu as promis aux polythéistes.","explicationEn":"93. O Messenger, say: “O Lord, if you show me regarding these idolaters the punishment You have promised them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023093","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-92.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-94.html"},{"numVerset":94,"texteArabe":"رَبِّ فَلَا تَجْعَلْنِي فِي الْقَوْمِ الظَّالِمِينَ","tradPropre":"alors, Seigneur, ne me place pas parmi les gens injustes.","tradEn":"My Lord, then do not place me among the wrongdoing people.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô mon Seigneur, si tu les punis et que j’en suis témoin, fasses que je ne sois pas parmi eux afin que je ne sois pas atteint par leur punition.","explicationEn":"94. O Lord, if You punish them and I am witnessing that, do not make me amongst them so that I would be afflicted with the punishment that afflicts them”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023094","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-93.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-95.html"},{"numVerset":95,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّا عَلَىٰ أَنْ نُرِيَكَ مَا نَعِدُهُمْ لَقَادِرُونَ","tradPropre":"Nous sommes Capable, certes, de te montrer ce que Nous leur promettons.","tradEn":"And indeed, We are Able to show you what We have promised them.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous sommes certainement capable de te montrer le châtiment que Nous leur avons promis et de t’en faire un témoin. Ni cette prouesse ni aucune autre ne Nous est impossible","explicationEn":"95. I have power to make you witness and see the punishment I am promising them. I am not powerless to do this or anything else.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023095","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-94.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-96.html"},{"numVerset":96,"texteArabe":"ادْفَعْ بِالَّتِي هِيَ أَحْسَنُ السَّيِّئَةَ  نَحْنُ أَعْلَمُ بِمَا يَصِفُونَ","tradPropre":"Repousse le mal par ce qui est meilleur. Nous savons très bien ce qu'ils décrivent.","tradEn":"Repel, by [means of] what is best, [their] evil. We are most knowing of what they describe.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, repousse celui qui t’offense par la meilleure de tes vertus qui consiste à lui pardonner et à endurer patiemment ses offenses. Nous sommes le mieux au fait de leur polythéisme et de leur démenti ainsi que des accusations mensongères qu’ils t'adressent, comme la sorcellerie et la folie.","explicationEn":"96. O Messenger, repel the one who is bad to you by the characteristic which is better, namely turning away from him and being patient with his harm. I know best the associating partners and denial they describe, and the unbefitting things they describe you with such as magic and insanity.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023096","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-95.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-97.html"},{"numVerset":97,"texteArabe":"وَقُلْ رَبِّ أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنْ هَمَزَاتِ الشَّيَاطِينِ","tradPropre":"Et dis: «Seigneur, je cherche Ta protection, contre les incitations des diables.","tradEn":"And say, \"My Lord, I seek refuge in You from the incitements of the devils,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Dis ensuite: Ô mon Seigneur, je cherche refuge auprès de toi contre les insufflations des démons.","explicationEn":"97. And say: “O Lord, I seek protection in You against the evil suggestions of the satans and their whisperings.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023097","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-96.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-98.html"},{"numVerset":98,"texteArabe":"وَأَعُوذُ بِكَ رَبِّ أَنْ يَحْضُرُونِ","tradPropre":"et je cherche Ta protection, Seigneur, contre leur présence auprès de moi».","tradEn":"And I seek refuge in You, my Lord, lest they be present with me.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Je cherche refuge auprès de toi, ô mon Seigneur, contre leur présence, lorsque j’accomplis une œuvre quelconque.","explicationEn":"98. And I seek refuge in You that they should be present with me in any of my affairs”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023098","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-97.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-99.html"},{"numVerset":99,"texteArabe":"حَتَّىٰ إِذَا جَاءَ أَحَدَهُمُ الْمَوْتُ قَالَ رَبِّ ارْجِعُونِ","tradPropre":"...Puis, lorsque la mort vient à l'un deux, il dit: «Mon Seigneur! Fais-moi revenir (sur terre),","tradEn":"[For such is the state of the disbelievers] until, when death comes to one of them, he says, \"My Lord, send me back","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Quand la mort se présente à l’un de ces polythéistes et que ce dernier voit de ses yeux sa punition, il éprouve du regret pour ce qu’il n’a pas accompli durant sa vie et pour ses manquements envers Allah. Il dira alors: Ô mon Seigneur, fais-moi revenir dans le bas monde.","explicationEn":"99. Until when death comes to one of these idolaters and he sees what is going to befall him, he says regretfully over his life that has escaped him and his deficiency regarding Allah: “O Lord, return me to the worldly life.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023099","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-98.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-100.html"},{"numVerset":100,"texteArabe":"لَعَلِّي أَعْمَلُ صَالِحًا فِيمَا تَرَكْتُ  كَلَّا  إِنَّهَا كَلِمَةٌ هُوَ قَائِلُهَا  وَمِنْ وَرَائِهِمْ بَرْزَخٌ إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُونَ","tradPropre":"afin que je fasse du bien dans ce que je délaissais». Non, c'est simplement une parole qu'il dit. Derrière eux, cependant, il y a une barrière, jusqu'au jour où ils seront ressuscités».","tradEn":"That I might do righteousness in that which I left behind.\" No! It is only a word he is saying; and behind them is a barrier until the Day they are resurrected.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il se peut que j’y accomplisse de bonnes œuvres. Non, tu n’obtiendras pas ce que tu demandes car ce ne sont que des paroles vaines. Si on faisait retourner un tel homme dans le bas monde, il ne tiendrait pas cette promesse et les gens comme lui, resterons dans un monde intermédiaire entre le bas monde et l’au-delà jusqu’à l’avènement du Jour de la Ressuscitation. Ils ne retourneront donc pas dans le bas monde afin de rattraper leurs erreurs et de corriger leurs fautes.","explicationEn":"100. Perhaps I will do good actions when I return to it. Never. The matter is not as you requested. It is only a statement he is uttering. If he were to return to the worldly life, he would not fulfil what he promised. These people who have died will remain in a barrier between the world and the afterlife until the Day of Resurrection and rising. Thus, they will not return from it to the world, to make up for what they lost and to correct what they spoiled.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023100","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-99.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-101.html"},{"numVerset":101,"texteArabe":"فَإِذَا نُفِخَ فِي الصُّورِ فَلَا أَنْسَابَ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ وَلَا يَتَسَاءَلُونَ","tradPropre":"Puis quand on soufflera dans la Trompe, il n'y aura plus de parenté entre eux ce jour là, et ils ne se poseront pas de questions.","tradEn":"So when the Horn is blown, no relationship will there be among them that Day, nor will they ask about one another.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Par un autre pour lui venir en aide. Ou : nul ne sera interrogé par un autre.","explicationUnanime":"Lorsque l’ange chargé de souffler dans la Trompe soufflera pour la seconde fois, marquant ainsi le début des évènements de la Résurrection, ils oublieront les liens de parenté dont ils s’enorgueillaient dans le bas monde et ils ne s’interrogeront pas les uns les autres, tout absorbés par ce qu’ils vivront.","explicationEn":"101. Then when the angel appointed to blow the Trumpet will blow the second time which will announce the Day of Judgment, there will be no relations between them to boast through, due to their being engrossed in the horrors of the Hearafter, and they will not question one another due to their being engrossed in what concerns them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023101","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-100.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-102.html"},{"numVerset":102,"texteArabe":"فَمَنْ ثَقُلَتْ مَوَازِينُهُ فَأُولَائِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُونَ","tradPropre":"Ceux dont la balance est lourde seront les bienheureux;","tradEn":"And those whose scales are heavy [with good deeds] - it is they who are the successful.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ceux dont les bonnes actions pèseront plus lourd que les mauvaises, auront réussi. Ils obtiendront ce qu’ils recherchaient et échapperont à ce qu’ils redoutaient.","explicationEn":"102. So whoever’s scales are heavy because of his good actions outweighing his bad actions, those are the successful ones, by attaining their objective and being saved from their fears.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023102","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-101.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-103.html"},{"numVerset":103,"texteArabe":"وَمَنْ خَفَّتْ مَوَازِينُهُ فَأُولَائِكَ الَّذِينَ خَسِرُوا أَنْفُسَهُمْ فِي جَهَنَّمَ خَالِدُونَ","tradPropre":"et ceux dont la balance est légère seront ceux qui ont ruiné leurs propres âmes et ils demeureront éternellement dans l'Enfer.","tradEn":"But those whose scales are light - those are the ones who have lost their souls, [being] in Hell, abiding eternally.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Quant à ceux dont les bonnes actions pèseront plus léger que les mauvaises, ils auront perdu leurs propres âmes pour avoir agi d’une manière qui était préjudiciable pour eux-mêmes et pour s’être abstenu de croire et d’accomplir de bonnes œuvres. Ils resteront éternellement dans le Feu de l’Enfer et n’en sortiront pas.","explicationEn":"103. And whoever’s scales are light because of his bad deeds outweighing his good deeds, those are the ones who have wasted themselves by doing that which is harmful to them, i.e., disbelief and sins, and leaving faith and good actions that were beneficial for them. They will be in the fire of hell forever and will not come out of it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023103","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-102.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-104.html"},{"numVerset":104,"texteArabe":"تَلْفَحُ وُجُوهَهُمُ النَّارُ وَهُمْ فِيهَا كَالِحُونَ","tradPropre":"Le feu brûlera leurs visages et ils auront les lèvres crispées.","tradEn":"The Fire will sear their faces, and they therein will have taut smiles.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Leurs visages seront brûlés par le feu et leurs lèvres se rétracteront au-dessus de leurs dents tellement ils seront renfrognés.","explicationEn":"104. The fire will burn their faces. Therein, their top and bottom lips will shrink away from their teeth, due to severe frowning.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023104","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-103.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-105.html"},{"numVerset":105,"texteArabe":"أَلَمْ تَكُنْ آيَاتِي تُتْلَىٰ عَلَيْكُمْ فَكُنْتُمْ بِهَا تُكَذِّبُونَ","tradPropre":"«Mes versets ne vous étaient-ils pas récités et vous les traitiez alors de mensonges?»","tradEn":"[It will be said], \"Were not My verses recited to you and you used to deny them?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"On leur dira sur un ton réprobateur: Ne vous récitait-on pas les versets d’Allah et ne les démentiez-vous pas?","explicationEn":"105. It will be said to rebuke them: “Were the verses of the Qur’ān not recited to you in the world but you used to deny them?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023105","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-104.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-106.html"},{"numVerset":106,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا رَبَّنَا غَلَبَتْ عَلَيْنَا شِقْوَتُنَا وَكُنَّا قَوْمًا ضَالِّينَ","tradPropre":"Ils dirent: «Seigneur! Notre malheur nous a vaincus, et nous étions des gens égarés.","tradEn":"They will say, \"Our Lord, our wretchedness overcame us, and we were a people astray.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils répondront: Ô notre Seigneur, notre destin malheureux nous a condamnés à être des gens égarés de la vérité.","explicationEn":"106. They will say: “Our Lord, our wretchedness which had already passed in Your knowledge overcame us, and we were a people astray from the truth.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023106","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-105.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-107.html"},{"numVerset":107,"texteArabe":"رَبَّنَا أَخْرِجْنَا مِنْهَا فَإِنْ عُدْنَا فَإِنَّا ظَالِمُونَ","tradPropre":"Seigneur, fais nous-en sortir! Et si nous récidivons, nous serons alors des injustes».","tradEn":"Our Lord, remove us from it, and if we were to return [to evil], we would indeed be wrongdoers.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô notre Seigneur, fais-nous sortir du feu et si nous retournons à la mécréance et à l’égarement, nous commettrions une injustice envers nous-mêmes et nous n’aurions alors plus d’excuse.","explicationEn":"107. Our Lord, take us out of the fire. If we return to the disbelief and misguidance we were upon, we will surely have wronged ourselves and our excuse will be broken”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023107","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-106.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-108.html"},{"numVerset":108,"texteArabe":"قَالَ اخْسَئُوا فِيهَا وَلَا تُكَلِّمُونِ","tradPropre":"Il dit: «Soyez-y refoulés (humiliés) et ne Me parlez plus».","tradEn":"He will say, \"Remain despised therein and do not speak to Me.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allah dira: Habitez l’Enfer, soyez-y avilis et humiliés et ne M’adressez plus la parole.","explicationEn":"108. Allah will say: “Sit in the fire and stay in there disgraced; never speak to me.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023108","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-107.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-109.html"},{"numVerset":109,"texteArabe":"إِنَّهُ كَانَ فَرِيقٌ مِنْ عِبَادِي يَقُولُونَ رَبَّنَا آمَنَّا فَاغْفِرْ لَنَا وَارْحَمْنَا وَأَنْتَ خَيْرُ الرَّاحِمِينَ","tradPropre":"Il y eut un groupe de Mes serviteurs qui dirent: «Seigneur, nous croyons; pardonne-nous donc et fais-nous miséricorde, car Tu es le meilleur des Miséricordieux»","tradEn":"Indeed, there was a party of My servants who said, 'Our Lord, we have believed, so forgive us and have mercy upon us, and You are the best of the merciful.'","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Certains de Mes serviteurs qui croyaient en Moi diront: Ô notre Seigneur, nous croyons en Toi. Pardonne-nous donc nos péchés et couvre-nous de Ta miséricorde, car Tu es le meilleur des miséricordieux.","explicationEn":"109. There was a group of My servants who believed in Me, saying: ‘Our Lord, we have believed in You, so forgive our sins and grant us Your mercy, and You are the best of those who show mercy’","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023109","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-108.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-110.html"},{"numVerset":110,"texteArabe":"فَاتَّخَذْتُمُوهُمْ سِخْرِيًّا حَتَّىٰ أَنْسَوْكُمْ ذِكْرِي وَكُنْتُمْ مِنْهُمْ تَضْحَكُونَ","tradPropre":"mais vous les avez pris en raillerie jusqu'à oublier de M'invoquer, et vous vous riiez d'eux.","tradEn":"But you took them in mockery to the point that they made you forget My remembrance, and you used to laugh at them.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Railliez-vous ces croyants qui invoquaient leur Seigneur et votre seule occupation n’était-elle pas de les tourner en dérision et de vous moquer d’eux au point que vous en avez oublié d’évoquer Allah?","explicationEn":"110. You took these believers who called upon their Lord as a joke, mocking them and making fun of them, until being engrossed in mocking them made you forget Allah’s remembrance and you used to laugh at them, jokingly and mockingly.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023110","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-109.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-111.html"},{"numVerset":111,"texteArabe":"إِنِّي جَزَيْتُهُمُ الْيَوْمَ بِمَا صَبَرُوا أَنَّهُمْ هُمُ الْفَائِزُونَ","tradPropre":"Vraiment, Je les ai récompensés aujourd'hui pour ce qu'ils ont enduré; et ce sont eux les triomphants.","tradEn":"Indeed, I have rewarded them this Day for their patient endurance - that they are the attainers [of success].\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"J’ai rétribué ces croyants en les faisant entrer au Paradis le Jour de la Résurrection pour avoir été patients dans leur obéissance à Allah et pour avoir enduré ces persécutions.","explicationEn":"111. I rewarded these believers with success through paradise on the Day of Judgment, due to their patience on Allah’s obedience and the harm they used to receive from you”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023111","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-110.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-112.html"},{"numVerset":112,"texteArabe":"قَالَ كَمْ لَبِثْتُمْ فِي الْأَرْضِ عَدَدَ سِنِينَ","tradPropre":"Il dira: «Combien d'années êtes-vous restés sur terre?»","tradEn":"[Allāh] will say, \"How long did you remain on earth in number of years?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allah dira: Combien d’années êtes-vous restés sur Terre et quel est le temps que vous y avez vainement perdu?","explicationEn":"112. He will say: “How many years did you spend on earth? And how much time did you waste therein?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023112","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-111.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-113.html"},{"numVerset":113,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا لَبِثْنَا يَوْمًا أَوْ بَعْضَ يَوْمٍ فَاسْأَلِ الْعَادِّينَ","tradPropre":"Ils diront: «Nous y avons demeuré un jour, ou une partie d'un jour. Interroge donc ceux qui comptent.»","tradEn":"They will say, \"We remained a day or part of a day; ask those who enumerate.\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Les anges, selon certains commentateurs.","explicationUnanime":"Ils répondront: Nous ne sommes restés qu’un jour ou moins d’un jour. Questionne donc ceux qui s’appliquent à calculer les durées en jours et en mois.","explicationEn":"113. They will reply by saying: “We stayed for one day or part of a day, so ask those who pay attention to counting days and months”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023113","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-112.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-114.html"},{"numVerset":114,"texteArabe":"قَالَ إِنْ لَبِثْتُمْ إِلَّا قَلِيلًا  لَوْ أَنَّكُمْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ","tradPropre":"Il dira: «Vous n'y avez demeuré que peu [de temps], si seulement vous saviez.","tradEn":"He will say, \"You stayed not but a little - if only you had known.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Autre sens : si seulement vous aviez su (le caractère éphémère de cette vie, vous ne l’auriez pas préférée à la vie éternelle).","explicationUnanime":"Allah leur dira: Vous n’êtes resté que peu de temps et il vous aurait été facile d’être patient et de m’obéir lors de cette courte durée, si vous connaissiez vraiment cette durée.","explicationEn":"114. He will say: “You only stayed in the world for a short period, in which it was easy to persevere upon obedience, if only you knew the length of your stay”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023114","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-113.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-115.html"},{"numVerset":115,"texteArabe":"أَفَحَسِبْتُمْ أَنَّمَا خَلَقْنَاكُمْ عَبَثًا وَأَنَّكُمْ إِلَيْنَا لَا تُرْجَعُونَ","tradPropre":"Pensiez-vous que Nous vous avions créés sans but, et que vous ne seriez pas ramenés vers Nous?»","tradEn":"Then did you think that We created you uselessly and that to Us you would not be returned?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô gens, croyez-vous que Nous vous avons créés vainement sans raison et que, comme les animaux, vous n’aurez droit ni à une récompense ni à une punition? Croyez-vous que vous ne retournerez pas auprès de Nous le Jour de la Résurrection afin de rendre des comptes et être rétribués?","explicationEn":"115. So do you think, O people, that I created you as a plaything without any wisdom, so that there will be no reward or punishment as with animals, and that you will not return to Me on the Day of Judgment for the reckoning and recompense?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023115","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-114.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-116.html"},{"numVerset":116,"texteArabe":"فَتَعَالَى اللَّهُ الْمَلِكُ الْحَقُّ  لَا إِلَاهَ إِلَّا هُوَ رَبُّ الْعَرْشِ الْكَرِيمِ","tradPropre":"Que soit exalté Allah, le vrai Souverain! Pas de divinité en dehors de Lui, le Seigneur du Trône sublime!","tradEn":"So exalted is Allāh, the Sovereign, the Truth; there is no deity except Him, Lord of the Noble Throne.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Que soit élevé Allah, le Souverain, Celui qui dispose de Sa Création comme Il l’entend, le Vrai, Celui dont la promesse est véridique et les paroles sont véridiques. Il n’existe pas de dieu méritant d’être adoré hormis Lui, le Seigneur du Noble Trône qui est la plus éminente des créatures. Or le Seigneur de la plus éminente des créatures est à plus forte raison le Seigneur du reste des créatures.","explicationEn":"116. So pure is Allah, the King, who does as He wishes with His creation, and Who Himself is True, His promise is true and His saying is true. There is no true deity besides Him, Lord of the Noble Throne which is the biggest creation. He Who is Lord of the biggest creation is Lord of all the creation.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023116","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-115.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-117.html"},{"numVerset":117,"texteArabe":"وَمَنْ يَدْعُ مَعَ اللَّهِ إِلَاهًا آخَرَ لَا بُرْهَانَ لَهُ بِهِ فَإِنَّمَا حِسَابُهُ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِ  إِنَّهُ لَا يُفْلِحُ الْكَافِرُونَ","tradPropre":"Et quiconque invoque avec Allah une autre divinité, sans avoir la preuve évidente [de son existence], aura à en rendre compte à son Seigneur. En vérité, les mécréants, ne réussiront pas.","tradEn":"And whoever invokes besides Allāh another deity for which he has no proof - then his account is only with his Lord. Indeed, the disbelievers will not succeed.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Quiconque invoque avec Allah un autre dieu sans détenir la preuve que ce dernier mérite d’être adoré, sera rétribué pour ce mauvais agissement en étant châtié. Les mécréants n’obtiendront pas ce qu’ils recherchent et n’échapperont pas à ce qu’ils redoutent.","explicationEn":"117. Whoever calls upon another god besides Allah for which he has no proof (and this is the case with every god besides Allah), the reward of his bad action is with his Lord, as He is the One Who will reward him for it by punishing him. The disbelievers will not be successful in attaining what they desire and being saved from their fears.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023117","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-116.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-23-verset-118.html"},{"numVerset":118,"texteArabe":"وَقُلْ رَبِّ اغْفِرْ وَارْحَمْ وَأَنْتَ خَيْرُ الرَّاحِمِينَ","tradPropre":"Et dis: «Seigneur, pardonne et fais miséricorde. C'est Toi le Meilleur des miséricordieux».","tradEn":"And, [O Muḥammad], say, \"My Lord, forgive and have mercy, and You are the best of the merciful.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, dis: Ô mon Seigneur, pardonne-moi mes péchés et couvre-moi de Ta miséricorde car Tu es le Meilleur de ceux qui font miséricorde à un serviteur et accepte son repentir.","explicationEn":"118. Say - O Messenger: “O Lord, forgive my sins, grant me Your mercy, and You are the best of those who show mercy”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"023118","lienPrecedent":"sourate-23-verset-117.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-24-verset-1.html"}]};